(window.AeroSenseTranslations ||= []).push({"Sustainable Development Impact":"永續發展影響","Trace the benefits, costs, and trade-offs.":"追溯效益、成本與取捨。","01 · Our approach":"01 · 我們的方法","AeroSense links a living olfactory-receptor layer, custom fluorescence readout and a fly-inspired classifier. Sustainability asks whether that system improves a real food decision, who benefits, and what resources it consumes. Our":"AeroSense 連結活體嗅覺受體層、客製化螢光讀取與受果蠅啟發的分類器。永續性所問的是：此系統是否改善真實的食品決策、誰受益，以及它耗用什麼資源。我們的","Human Practices work":"人文實踐工作","guides that question; every potential benefit below is paired with a limitation and a next measurement.":"引導這項提問；下方每個潛在效益，都搭配限制與下一步量測。","Ecological, social and economic systems belong together":"生態、社會與經濟系統必須一起考量","The Brundtland framework asks us to meet present needs while preserving future generations’ ability to meet theirs. For AeroSense, that means considering food loss, affordability and the footprint of the device together.":"布倫特蘭架構要求我們滿足當代需求，同時保留未來世代滿足自身需求的能力。對 AeroSense 而言，這代表同時考量食品損失、可負擔性與設備足跡。","Systems thinking helps us follow consequences beyond the sensor: a useful alert could reduce late discard, while cartridges add waste or pricing excludes smaller producers. Resilience means retaining a useful function as conditions change.":"系統思考幫助我們追蹤感測器以外的後果：有用的警示可能減少後期丟棄，但匣體也會增加廢棄物，定價也可能排除小型生產者。韌性意味著在條件改變時，仍能保留有用功能。","We use the UN Sustainable Development Goals to organize these connected questions.":"我們使用聯合國永續發展目標，整理這些彼此連動的問題。","Two application tracks share a sensing stack, but require separate evidence.":"兩條應用路線共用感測架構，但需要各自的證據。","Track A · Export supply chain":"路線 A · 出口供應鏈","Track B · Stored food":"路線 B · 儲存食品","Intended decision":"預期支持的決策","Earlier disease, ripeness and quality triage for banana and mango lots; tea is a later extension.":"更早對香蕉與芒果批次的病害、熟度及品質進行分流；茶葉是較後期的延伸。","Screen pathogen- or mold-associated VOCs in stored food and communicate when confirmation is needed.":"篩檢儲存食品中與病原體或黴菌相關的 VOCs，並說明何時需要確認。","Evidence today":"目前證據","Agricultural-institution interviews and mentor review. Banana is the narrowed commercial beachhead; exporters and packing houses have not yet been interviewed.":"農業機構訪談與導師審查。香蕉是已縮小的商業灘頭堡方向；出口商與包裝場尚未受訪。","Laboratory development and an early survey summary (n = 28). A later total of 107 is team reported; updated item-level results are unavailable.":"實驗室開發與早期問卷摘要（n = 28）。後期總數 107 是團隊回報；無更新的逐題結果。","Next evidence":"下一步證據","Batch-level loss records, detection lead time and a cost model showing who pays and who benefits.":"批次層級損失記錄、偵測提前時間，以及說明誰付費、誰受益的成本模型。","Verified survey counts, validated screening performance and user tests of risk-tier communication.":"核實的問卷人數、經驗證的篩檢效能，以及風險分級溝通的使用者測試。","Claim boundary":"主張範圍","No measured shipment-loss reduction, paid pilot or demonstrated field performance.":"尚無實測貨運損失減少、付費試點或已展示的現場效能。","No food-safety verdict, mycotoxin certification or population-wide conclusion from the survey.":"不提供食品安全判定、真菌毒素認證，也不從問卷推論整體人口。","What we include":"納入哪些部分","Living OR/Orco + reporter cell cartridge, ESP32 FDM/DLIA reader, neuromorphic classification stack.":"活體 OR／Orco 加報導蛋白的細胞匣體、ESP32 FDM／DLIA 讀取器，以及神經形態分類架構。","Wet-lab consumables, culture media, and single-use plastics used to build and test the sensing layer.":"建構與測試感測層所使用的濕實驗耗材、培養基與一次性塑膠。","Agricultural institutions already interviewed (stations, associations, facility farms) and the confirmatory lab chain a screen is meant to feed.":"已訪談的農業機構（改良場、協會／農會、設施農場），以及篩檢預期銜接的確認實驗室流程。","Desired buyers in Track A: exporters / packing houses —":"路線 A 的期望買方：出口商／包裝場——","not yet interviewed directly":"尚未直接訪談","What remains unvalidated":"哪些仍未驗證","Clinical diagnosis or medical-device claims.":"臨床診斷或醫療器材主張。","Mycotoxin certification or definitive food-safety verdicts.":"真菌毒素認證或明確的食品安全判定。","Sealed field pilots, contracted LOIs, or measured shipment-loss reduction.":"密封場域試點、已簽約意向書，或實測貨運損失減少。","A completed product LCA or priced manufacturing COGS.":"完整產品生命週期評估，或具有實際報價的製造銷貨成本。","02 · Four goals":"02 · 四項目標","The four primary goals connect our design choices to specific targets. The next test matters as much as the proposed benefit.":"四項主要目標，將設計選擇連結至具體細項目標。下一步測試，與提議的效益同樣重要。","Resilient agriculture and smallholder income":"韌性農業與小農所得","Targets 2.4 / 2.3.":"細項目標 2.4／2.3。","Earlier VOC triage could support batch isolation or rerouting. Shared institutional access could reduce the need for individual farmers to buy a reader.":"較早的 VOC 分流可能支持批次隔離或改道處理。機構共用設備，可能降低個別農民購買讀取器的需求。","Next:":"下一步：","interview an exporter or packing house, measure lead time, and trace who receives the economic benefit.":"訪談出口商或包裝場、量測提前時間，並追蹤誰取得經濟效益。","Biological sensing and local technology":"生物感測與在地技術","Targets 9.5 / 9.b.":"細項目標 9.5／9.b。","Living OR/Orco cells, a team-designed ESP32 reader and fly-inspired classification form our research approach.":"活體 OR／Orco 細胞、團隊設計的 ESP32 讀取器與果蠅啟發分類，構成我們的研究方法。","complete staged validation and measure power across the reader and recurring biological workflow.":"完成分階段驗證，並量測讀取器與反覆進行的生物流程所需的功耗。","Food decisions, reuse and our own waste":"食品決策、重用與我們自身的廢棄物","Targets 12.3 / 12.5 / 12.4.":"細項目標 12.3／12.5／12.4。","Headspace sampling aims to preserve the food sample. Cartridge reuse and clearer risk information remain design intentions.":"頂空採樣旨在保留食品樣品。匣體重用與更清楚的風險資訊，仍是設計意圖。","test cartridge lifetime, audit laboratory consumables, and compare complete workflows in a screening LCA.":"測試匣體壽命、盤點實驗室耗材，並以初步生命週期評估比較完整流程。","Knowledge-sharing with clear maturity":"清楚標示成熟程度的知識共享","Targets 17.16 / 17.17.":"細項目標 17.16／17.17。","Field interviews, industry advice, academic collaboration and mentorship have shaped the project.":"實地訪談、產業建議、學術合作與導師指導，塑造了專案。","conduct the prepared company visit and document whether it develops into a formal collaboration.":"執行已準備的公司參訪，並記錄是否發展為正式合作。","Supporting connections:":"支持性連結：","SDG 3 · health-protective screening":"SDG 3 · 保護健康的篩檢","SDG 10 · access and affordability":"SDG 10 · 可近性與可負擔性","We have no measured food-loss reduction, cartridge lifetime, net environmental benefit or operating-power result. The":"我們尚無食品損失減少、匣體壽命、淨環境效益或操作功耗的實測結果。","evidence ledger":"證據清單","distinguishes observations, stakeholder input, estimates, designs and open questions.":"區分觀察、利害關係人意見、估計、設計與未解問題。","Follow the evidence":"跟隨證據","1 · Follow a food decision":"1 · 跟隨一個食品決策","Where the screen would enter a real workflow.":"篩檢會在實際工作流程的哪裡介入。","2 · Learn from stakeholders":"2 · 向利害關係人學習","What we heard and what changed.":"我們聽到了什麼，以及改變了什麼。","3 · Examine each goal":"3 · 檢視每項目標","Mechanism, evidence, tension and next measurement.":"機制、證據、矛盾與下一步量測。","4 · Measure our contribution":"4 · 量測我們的貢獻","Baselines, targets and evidence still needed.":"基準、目標與仍需補足的證據。","System map":"系統地圖","Sustainability effects, if any, would appear along a decision chain — not inside an SDG icon. Select a stage or actor to see what happens there, who is involved, what could be gained or lost, and what evidence we actually have. Engagement labels are deliberate: interviews are not commercial partnerships.":"永續影響如果存在，會出現在決策鏈上，而不是 SDG 圖示裡。選擇階段或行動者，查看該處發生什麼、涉及誰、可能獲得或損失什麼，以及我們實際有哪些證據。接觸狀態的標籤經過刻意區分：訪談不是商業合作。","Stages run left to right on wide screens and top to bottom on small screens. Keyboard: Tab to a node, Enter or Space to open its detail.":"寬螢幕由左至右，小螢幕由上至下。鍵盤操作：以 Tab 移至節點，按 Enter 或空白鍵開啟詳情。","Food / produce":"食品／農產品","Crop or stored goods enter the decision system":"作物或儲存物品進入決策系統","VOC change":"VOC 變化","Headspace chemistry may shift before symptoms":"頂空化學組成可能在症狀前改變","AeroSense screening":"AeroSense 篩檢","Cartridge + ESP32 reader — designed, not field-proven":"匣體＋ESP32 讀取器：已設計，尚未經現場驗證","Risk information":"風險資訊","Tiered output — not a silent “safe”":"分級輸出，不是無說明的「安全」","Human / institutional decision":"人／機構的決策","Isolate, confirm, ship, hold, or discard":"隔離、確認、出貨、暫存或丟棄","Outcome":"成果","Loss avoided, waste created, or trust broken — all still hypothesized":"避免損失、產生廢棄物，或破壞信任：目前皆為假設","Actors along the chain":"鏈上的行動者","Producer / farm":"生產者／農場","Stakeholder engaged":"已接觸利害關係人","Facility farms interviewed":"已訪談設施農場","Cooperative / farmers’ association":"合作社／農會","Associations + stations interviewed":"已訪談協會／農會與改良場","Packing / storage / logistics":"包裝／儲存／物流","Not yet interviewed":"尚未訪談","Desired Track A buyers — open gap":"期望的路線 A 買方：仍是缺口","Analytical laboratory":"分析實驗室","Confirmatory-testing interview 2026-09-13":"確認性檢測訪談：2026-09-13","Consumer / downstream food system":"消費者／下游食品系統","Proposed user":"預定使用者","Early survey n = 28; later total 107; not buyer evidence":"早期問卷 n = 28；後期總數 107；不是買方證據","01 · Food / produce":"01 · 食品／農產品","What happens here":"這裡發生什麼","Banana, mango, tea, or stored food enters a handling chain where quality, disease, or spoilage risk will eventually force a decision.":"香蕉、芒果、茶葉或儲存食品，進入一條最終會因品質、病害或腐敗風險而必須做出決策的處理鏈。","Relevant stakeholder":"相關利害關係人","Producers and facility farms (engaged); exporters and packing houses (not yet interviewed).":"生產者與設施農場（已接觸）；出口商與包裝場（尚未訪談）。","Potential sustainability gain":"潛在永續效益","Earlier attention to lots that will otherwise spread loss or trigger over-discard later in the chain.":"更早注意到那些否則可能在後續鏈中擴大損失，或造成過度丟棄的批次。","Possible negative consequence":"可能的負面後果","If screening never reaches this stage’s real owners, “resilience” stays a desk story and smallholders may still bear cost without benefit.":"若篩檢始終未接觸此階段真正負責的人，「韌性」就只是紙上故事，小農仍可能只負擔成本卻未受益。","Relevant SDG targets":"相關 SDG 細項目標","2.4 resilient practices; 12.3 food loss along supply chains.":"2.4 韌性實務；12.3 供應鏈中的食品損失。","Evidence status":"證據狀態","Stakeholder-backed":"利害關係人意見","pain framing ·":"的痛點定位 ·","exporter workflow":"出口商工作流程","Entrepreneurship · Decision problem":"創業 · 決策問題","Sustainability · SDG 2":"永續 · SDG 2","02 · VOC change":"02 · VOC 變化","Fungal disease, ripeness, or spoilage chemistry may alter volatile organic compounds in the headspace before surface symptoms are obvious.":"真菌病害、熟度或腐敗化學變化，可能在表面症狀明顯前，就改變頂空中的揮發性有機化合物。","Plant-protection and farm interviewees who described asymptomatic spread; wet-lab / Parts panel for receptor hypotheses.":"描述無症狀傳播的植物保護與農場受訪者；提供受體假說的濕實驗／元件面板。","A detectable early signal could move decisions upstream of visual triage.":"可偵測的早期訊號，可能把決策時點移到目視分流之前。","Assuming VOC presence “for days” without kinetics data; mistaking mold VOC for mycotoxin presence.":"在缺乏動態資料時，假設 VOC 已存在「好幾天」；將黴菌 VOC 誤認為真菌毒素存在。","2.4; 9.5 (sensing capability); 3 (claim discipline on toxins).":"2.4；9.5（感測能力）；3（毒素主張的紀律）。","Hypothesis":"假設","for AeroSense-detectable disease VOC ·":"：AeroSense 可偵測的病害 VOC ·","problem timing narrative":"問題時序敘述","Sustainability · SDG 3":"永續 · SDG 3","03 · AeroSense screening":"03 · AeroSense 篩檢","Living OR/Orco + reporter cartridge is read by an ESP32-standalone FDM/DLIA optical front end. Architecture designed; fabrication and validation ladder pending.":"以 ESP32 獨立運作的 FDM／DLIA 光學前端，讀取活體 OR／Orco 加報導蛋白匣體。架構已設計，製造與驗證階梯仍待完成。","Hardware / dry-lab team; e-nose CSO interview on sensing-element limits; Safety oversight for live cells.":"硬體／乾實驗團隊；討論感測元件限制的電子鼻 CSO 訪談；活細胞工作的安全監督。","Non-destructive headspace screen intended to reduce reliance on purely destructive sampling for every lot.":"非破壞性頂空篩檢，旨在減少每批都完全依賴破壞性採樣的需求。","Cartridge and culture waste; biosafety burden; energy and electronics footprint not yet measured.":"匣體與培養廢棄物、生物安全負擔，以及尚未量測的能源與電子設備足跡。","9.5 / 9.b; 12.4–12.5 (own waste).":"9.5／9.b；12.4–12.5（自身廢棄物）。","Designed":"設計","· power & field performance":"· 功耗與現場效能","Sustainability · SDG 9":"永續 · SDG 9","04 · Risk information":"04 · 風險資訊","Model and product framing aim for a risk":"模型與產品定位，旨在提供風險","tier":"等級","with escalation guidance — not a binary discard/don’t-discard or a silent safe label.":"，搭配升級處理指引，而非丟棄／不丟棄的二元選擇，或無說明的安全標籤。","Public survey (updated analysis pending); Challenge Bioproducts Co., Ltd. interview (VOC ≠ food-safety verdict); Education track.":"一般大眾問卷（更新分析待完成）；Challenge Bioproducts Co., Ltd. 訪談（VOC 不等於食品安全判定）；教育路線。","Could reduce over-caution discard and unsafe under-reaction if tiers are trusted appropriately.":"若適當信任分級結果，可能減少過度謹慎造成的丟棄，以及不安全的反應不足。","Overtrust of a low-risk tier could allow a false negative to delay confirmatory testing. Respondent priorities await verified item-level analysis.":"過度信任低風險等級，可能讓偽陰性延誤確認性檢測。填答者的優先考量仍待核實逐題分析。","12.3; 3 (health-protective claims).":"12.3；3（保護健康的主張）。","output form ·":"輸出形式 ·","Next validation":"下一步驗證","updated survey item analysis · outcome":"更新問卷逐題分析 · 結果","Education · Survey":"教育 · 問卷","Entrepreneurship · Responsible scaling":"創業 · 負責任的擴展","05 · Human / institutional decision":"05 · 人／機構的決策","A person or institution chooses isolate, confirmatory test, ship, hold, rework, or discard — under time and cost pressure.":"個人或機構在時間與成本壓力下，選擇隔離、確認性檢測、出貨、暫存、重新處理或丟棄。","Corrected buyer hypothesis: associations / stations / cooperatives / certifiers. Packing houses remain not yet interviewed.":"修正後的買方假說：協會／農會、改良場、合作社與認證單位。包裝場仍未受訪。","Shared institutional tools could protect smallholder lots without forcing individual purchase.":"機構共用工具，可能在不強迫個別購買的前提下，保護小農批次。","Value captured only by exporters; farmers resist tools that flag their product; access inequality.":"價值只由出口商取得；農民抗拒會標記自家產品問題的工具；取得機會不平等。","buyer correction · equity outcome":"買方修正 · 公平結果","Entrepreneurship · Who needs this":"創業 · 誰需要這個方案","Sustainability · Who benefits":"永續 · 誰受益","06 · Outcome":"06 · 結果","Food loss reduced, waste created, trust gained or broken, confirmatory labs busier or bypassed — depending on how the decision is used.":"食品損失減少、廢棄物增加、信任建立或破壞、確認實驗室更忙或被繞過，取決於決策如何被使用。","Entire chain, including downstream consumers and future regulators.":"整條鏈，包括下游消費者與未來監管者。","Hypothesized earlier isolation and less blind discard — not measured.":"假設能更早隔離、減少盲目丟棄；尚未量測。","Net environmental loss from cartridges; false-negative harm; SDG trade-offs listed in the map below.":"匣體可能造成淨環境損失、偽陰性傷害，以及下方地圖所列的 SDG 取捨。","2, 3, 9, 10, 12, 17 — interaction map.":"2、3、9、10、12、17：互動地圖。","· no pilot loss metrics · LCA":"· 無試點損失指標 · 生命週期評估","Sustainability · Trade-off map":"永續 · 取捨地圖","Actor · Producer / farm":"行動者 · 生產者／農場","Production and early post-harvest handling; disease and sampling practices begin on the ground.":"生產與採後初期處理；病害及採樣實務從現場開始。","Facility farms —":"設施農場——","stakeholder engaged":"已接觸利害關係人","via completed interviews. Individual smallholders are not the default buyer.":"，透過已完成的訪談。個別小農不是預設買方。","Shared institutional screening could protect incomes without requiring each farm to purchase a device.":"機構共用篩檢，可能在不要求每個農場購買設備的情況下保護所得。","Low willingness to pay; resistance to tools that flag one’s own product (analytical interview).":"付費意願低；抗拒會標記自家產品問題的工具（分析儀器訪談）。","Sustainability · Stakeholder changes":"永續 · 利害關係人帶來的改變","Entrepreneurship · Traction":"創業 · 進展","Actor · Cooperative / farmers’ association":"行動者 · 合作社／農會","Collective QC, advice, and potential shared tooling between farms and markets.":"農場與市場之間的集體品質管制、建議，以及潛在共用工具。","Local farmers’ associations and Taoyuan District Agricultural Improvement Station Plant Protection Lab —":"地方農會與桃園區農業改良場植物保護研究室——","Institution-level adoption is the current design response to farmer-side WTP and equity risks.":"機構層級採用，是目前設計對農民端付費意願與公平風險的回應。","Capacity and cost may still exclude smaller associations; benefit may not flow to members.":"能力與成本仍可能排除較小型組織；效益也未必回到成員身上。","· outcome equity":"· 結果公平性","Sustainability · SDG 10":"永續 · SDG 10","Actor · Packing / storage / logistics":"行動者 · 包裝／儲存／物流","Lots are graded, packed, stored, and timed for shipment — the expensive decision point in the Track A beachhead hypothesis.":"批次分級、包裝、儲存並安排出貨時間：這是路線 A 灘頭堡假說中，成本高昂的決策點。","Banana/mango exporters and packing houses —":"香蕉／芒果出口商與包裝場——","not yet interviewed":"尚未訪談",". Prospective actors / proposed users, not completed partners.":"。他們是潛在行動者／預定使用者，不是已完成合作的夥伴。","Same-shift triage could reduce mixed-lot spread and late discard — hypothesized only.":"同一班次內的分流，可能減少混批傳播與後期丟棄；目前僅是假說。","Building a product for a buyer we have not spoken to; overclaiming beachhead readiness.":"為尚未交談的買方開發產品；過度宣稱灘頭堡市場已準備就緒。","Entrepreneurship · Beachhead":"創業 · 灘頭堡市場","Actor · Analytical laboratory":"行動者 · 分析實驗室","Confirmatory GC–MS / LC–MS / related assays resolve what a screen only flags.":"確認性的 GC–MS／LC–MS／相關試驗，解決篩檢僅能標記的問題。","Analytical-instrumentation industry professional —":"分析儀器產業專業人士——","(2026-09-13). Labs remain in the loop by design.":"（2026-09-13）。依設計，實驗室仍留在流程中。","Upstream screening could reserve destructive, high-skill assays for suspicious lots.":"上游篩檢可能將破壞性、需高度技能的試驗，集中保留給可疑批次。","Marketing that implies lab replacement; undercutting confirmatory discipline.":"暗示取代實驗室的行銷，會削弱確認程序的紀律。","positioning pivot":"定位轉向","Entrepreneurship · What we learned":"創業 · 我們學到什麼","Actor · Consumer / downstream food system":"行動者 · 消費者／下游食品系統","Downstream trust, discard habits, and food-safety misconceptions shape Track B education and claim language.":"下游信任、丟棄習慣與食品安全迷思，塑造路線 B 的教育與主張用語。","of safer information — not a B2B buyer. The early n = 28 summary is directional engagement. The later reported total of 107 has no supplied item-level analysis; neither is a customer contract.":"更安全資訊的受益者，而非 B2B 買方。早期 n = 28 摘要提供方向性的接觸資訊。後期回報總數 107，未提供逐題分析；兩者都不是客戶合約。","Less over-caution waste":"減少過度謹慎造成的浪費","if":"前提是","trustworthy triage exists; better mold-decision habits via Education.":"有可信賴的分流；透過教育改善與黴菌相關的決策習慣。","Treating a small survey as population proof; Unverified B2C price assumptions.":"將小型問卷當成人口證據；未驗證的 B2C 價格假設。","12.3; 3; Education (not an SDG badge).":"12.3；3；教育（不是 SDG 徽章）。","Early survey aggregate":"早期問卷彙整","directional · product impact":"提供方向 · 產品影響","Sustainability · SDG 12":"永續 · SDG 12","04 · Integration":"04 · 整合","Field, industry, academic and public perspectives changed the sensing strategy, buyer model and claim boundaries. Interviews, mentorship and research collaboration represent different kinds of progress; none establishes a contracted commercial partnership.":"實地、產業、學術與大眾觀點，改變了感測策略、買方模型與主張範圍。訪談、導師指導及研究合作代表不同進展，都不等於已簽約的商業合作。","Engagement":"接觸","Collaboration":"合作","Mentorship":"導師輔導","Prospective partnership":"潛在夥伴關係","Formal partnership":"正式夥伴關係","none claimed":"未宣稱有任何正式關係","Agricultural improvement station / plant-protection expertise":"農業改良場／植物保護專業","Taoyuan District Agricultural Improvement Station · Plant Protection Lab":"桃園區農業改良場 · 植物保護研究室","Before":"改變前","We assumed desk research could locate the post-harvest disease-detection pain point without field correction.":"我們原本假設，只靠資料研究，不經實地修正，也能找出採後病害偵測的痛點。","Upstream agricultural institutions helped identify where disease and post-harvest handling affect the chain. Exporter-side loss volumes still need direct validation.":"上游農業機構協助辨識，病害與採後處理如何影響整條鏈。出口商端的損失量仍需直接驗證。","Beachhead and economic framing anchored to agricultural supply-chain reality rather than a six-crop facility list.":"灘頭堡市場與經濟定位，立基於農業供應鏈現實，而不是六種設施作物的清單。","Where it appears in AeroSense":"在 AeroSense 中出現的位置","Track A candidate beachhead; Entrepreneurship decision problem; Sustainability SDG 2 pathway.":"路線 A 候選灘頭堡市場；創業決策問題；永續 SDG 2 路徑。","Current evidence status":"目前證據狀態","Discovery interview / site visit — not a device pilot.":"探索訪談／實地參訪，不是設備試點。","Human Practices · Integration cases":"人文實踐· 整合案例","Engagement timeline":"接觸時間軸","Farmers’ associations / facility farms":"農會／設施農場","Local associations and facility farms — completed interviews":"地方農會與設施農場：已完成訪談","Sampling and post-harvest handling were treated as background context rather than design constraints.":"採樣與採後處理原本被視為背景資訊，而非設計限制。","Sampling, handling and institutional access shape whether a screening tool can be useful to growers. These discussions support a shared-tool strategy.":"採樣、處理與機構取得管道，決定篩檢工具對種植者是否有用。這些討論支持共用工具策略。","Product and outreach language tied to institutional agricultural channels so screening need not require each farm to purchase a device. Stakeholder record:":"產品與對外溝通用語，連結至農業機構通路，使篩檢不必要求每個農場都購買設備。利害關係人記錄：","Buyer-segment correction; food-pathway actors; SDG 10 access discussion.":"買方區隔修正；食品路徑行動者；SDG 10 可近性討論。","· individual interviewee names not published":"· 未公布個別受訪者姓名","Human Practices · Stakeholder map":"人文實踐· 利害關係人地圖","Electronic-nose industry":"電子鼻產業","Chief Science Officer interview (identity pending confirmation before naming)":"科學長訪談（具名前仍待確認身分）","Differentiation risked sounding like “better electronics and algorithms.”":"差異化有流於「更好的電子與演算法」訴求的風險。","The sensing element remains a bottleneck: selectivity, sensitivity, lifetime and reproducibility determine whether an electronic nose is useful. This is a paraphrase of the interview.":"感測元件仍是瓶頸：選擇性、靈敏度、壽命與重現性，決定電子鼻是否有用。此處為訪談轉述。","Innovation effort placed on the living sensing element (SDG 9). Stakeholder record:":"將創新工作聚焦於活體感測元件（SDG 9）。利害關係人記錄：","Hardware / Parts narrative; SDG 9 pathway; Entrepreneurship alternatives framing.":"硬體／元件敘事；SDG 9 路徑；創業頁面的替代方案定位。","· paraphrase only ·":"· 僅為轉述 ·","Verify before publication":"發布前核實","for any verbatim quote":"任何逐字引言","A separate domestic e-nose company visit explored as a":"另一次國內電子鼻公司參訪，探索作為","is prepared but":"的可能性，已準備但","not conducted":"尚未進行","— not the same thing as this CSO engagement, and not a":"，與這次 CSO 接觸並非同一件事，也不是","Human Practices · Integration":"人文實踐· 整合","Biotechnology industry":"生物科技產業","Challenge Bioproducts Co., Ltd. · 2026-09-12":"Challenge Bioproducts Co., Ltd. · 2026-09-12","Mold-associated VOCs risked being marketed as food-safety verdicts.":"黴菌相關 VOC，有被行銷成食品安全判定的風險。","A VOC signal does not establish food safety. The interview highlighted that toxin risk can remain even when the original fungi are no longer viable.":"VOC 訊號不能確立食品安全。訪談指出，即使原來的真菌已失去活性，毒素風險仍可能存在。","Screening-not-diagnostic boundary hardened for health-protective claim discipline (SDG 3). Stakeholder record:":"強化「篩檢而非診斷」範圍，以維持保護健康的主張紀律（SDG 3）。利害關係人記錄：","Safety claim language; SDG 3 supporting pathway; Entrepreneurship beachhead matrix.":"安全主張用語；SDG 3 支持路徑；創業灘頭堡市場矩陣。","· paraphrase of interview synthesis":"· 訪談整理的轉述","Human Practices · Ethical analysis":"人文實踐· 倫理分析","Analytical-instrumentation industry":"分析儀器產業","GC–MS / LC–MS testing-service professional · 2026-09-13":"GC–MS／LC–MS 檢測服務專業人士 · 2026-09-13","Value proposition leaned on undercutting laboratory instrument cost.":"價值主張原本偏向壓低實驗室儀器成本。","Individual farmers may have low willingness to pay and may resist a tool that flags their own produce. Institutional buyers and confirmatory services therefore matter.":"個別農民可能付費意願低，也可能抗拒會標記自家農產品問題的工具，因此機構買方與確認服務很重要。","Buyer design moved toward associations, stations, cooperatives, and certifiers so screening is not locked to individual purchase (SDG 10). Stakeholder record:":"買方設計轉向協會／農會、改良場、合作社與認證單位，避免篩檢只能靠個別購買取得（SDG 10）。利害關係人記錄：","Entrepreneurship GTM; SDG 2.3 / SDG 10 equity tension; confirmatory-lab actor on the food pathway.":"創業市場進入策略；SDG 2.3／SDG 10 公平性矛盾；食品路徑上的確認實驗室。","· interviewee-reported cost figures are estimates, not AeroSense measurements":"· 受訪者回報的成本數字是估計值，不是 AeroSense 量測","Human Practices · How HP changed the project":"人文實踐· HP 如何改變專案","Academic advisors":"學術顧問","Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo (NTHU) · Prof. Ching-Che Charng (China Medical University)":"Chung-Chuan Lo 教授（清華大學）· Ching-Che Charng 教授（中國醫藥大學）","Neuromorphic classification risked reading as borrowed metaphor rather than grounded research lineage.":"神經形態分類原本可能被看成借用的比喻，而非有根據的研究脈絡。","See Evidence Ledger":"查看證據清單","(Decode /":"（解碼／","Science Advances":"Science Advances","lineage).":"研究脈絡）。","We cite a published research lineage for the computational approach — while refusing to equate that paper with AeroSense agri VOC accuracy.":"我們為運算方法引用已發表的研究脈絡，同時不將該論文等同於 AeroSense 的農業 VOC 準確率。","Model / Description Decode layer; SDG 9 evidence slot; Entrepreneurship capability narrative.":"模型／專案介紹的解碼層；SDG 9 證據位置；創業能力敘事。","authorship · paper results ≠ product performance":"作者關係 · 論文結果不等於產品效能","Food storage habits and mold risk perception · early n = 28 record: 23 August 2026 · later reported total: 107, date unconfirmed":"食品儲存習慣與黴菌風險認知 · 早期 n = 28 記錄：2026 年 8 月 23 日 · 後期回報總數：107，日期未確認","We assumed broad public misunderstanding of mold risk was the main education problem.":"我們原本假設，大眾普遍誤解黴菌風險，是主要教育問題。","The early survey informed questions about mold decisions and risk communication. Updated item-level counts are unavailable; the draft’s universal discard claim is not treated as a verified result.":"早期問卷引導了黴菌決策與風險溝通問題。更新的逐題人數無法取得；草稿中的普遍丟棄主張，不視為已驗證結果。","Education track redesign; product communication toward risk tiers rather than a silent “safe.”":"教育路線重新設計；產品溝通朝向風險等級，而非無說明的「安全」。","Education redesign":"教育重新設計","food-retention and safety trade-off":"食品保留與安全的取捨","responsible scaling":"負責任的擴展","Team-reported aggregate":"團隊回報彙整資料","· early n = 28;":"· 早期 n = 28；","counts and limits":"人數與限制",". The separate EL-02 discard claim is not used.":"。未使用另列的 EL-02 丟棄主張。","Human Practices · Engagement method":"人文實踐· 接觸方法","FITI / NTHU Garage+ mentors":"FITI／NTHU Garage+ 導師","11-point BP review 2026-08-27 · pitch-deck review 2026-09-07 · Garage+ 18th cohort":"商業計畫 11 點審查：2026-08-27 · 簡報審查：2026-09-07 · Garage+ 第 18 屆","Broad multi-crop platform sized against the global e-nose instrument market.":"廣泛多作物平台，原本以全球電子鼻儀器市場估算規模。","Mentor review called for a focused agricultural decision problem and a buyer-specific market model instead of a broad electronic-nose market claim.":"導師審查要求聚焦農業決策問題與特定買方市場模型，而非廣泛的電子鼻市場主張。","Banana disease-detection remains the commercial beachhead hypothesis used for Track A SDG 2 wording. Stakeholder record:":"香蕉病害偵測仍是商業灘頭堡假說，用於路線 A 的 SDG 2 敘述。利害關係人記錄：",". Market sizing:":"。市場規模估算：","Entrepreneurship beachhead and market sections; Sustainability Track A wording.":"創業頁面的灘頭堡與市場章節；永續頁面的路線 A 用語。","written mentor reviews · not a commercial contract":"導師書面審查，不是商業合約","Human Practices · Engagement timeline":"人文實踐· 接觸時間軸","05 · Pathways":"05 · 路徑","Each pathway uses the same logic: Target → Problem → AeroSense mechanism → Evidence → Boundary / risk → Next measurement. Empty evidence stays empty.":"每條路徑採用相同邏輯：目標 → 問題 → AeroSense 機制 → 證據 → 範圍／風險 → 下一步量測。空缺證據保持空缺。","SDG 2 — Zero Hunger":"SDG 2——消除飢餓","Track A primary":"路線 A 主要目標","Target":"目標","Target 2.4 — more resilient agricultural practices along the supply chain. Target 2.3 — smallholder productivity and incomes — is the tension we refuse to hide.":"目標 2.4：沿供應鏈建立更具韌性的農業實務。目標 2.3：小農生產力與所得，是我們不願隱藏的矛盾。","Problem":"問題","The proposed application is earlier disease and ripeness triage in banana and mango supply chains. The commercial plan currently narrows to banana disease screening. Visual inspection and laboratory confirmation enter different points in that workflow; their turnaround and cost must be measured with the intended buyer.":"提議的應用是更早對香蕉與芒果供應鏈的病害及熟度進行分流。目前商業計畫縮小為香蕉病害篩檢。目視檢查與實驗室確認在流程的不同位置介入；其處理時間與成本，必須與預定買方共同量測。","holds the market assumptions (":"列出市場假設（","Estimated":"估計","Mechanism":"機制","Designed VOC risk tiers that could inform isolate / reroute / time-shipment decisions before symptoms are obvious. This is an aim — not a demonstrated loss reduction.":"設計的 VOC 風險分級，可能在症狀明顯前，為隔離、改道或調整出貨時間提供依據。這是目標，不是已展示的損失減少。","Stakeholder and gap status:":"利害關係人與缺口狀態：","Boundary / risk":"主張範圍／風險","A tool that improves exporter resilience can still fail Target 2.3 if value never reaches smallholders — or if individual farmers resist a device that flags their own product (":"改善出口商韌性的工具，若價值始終未流向小農，或個別農民抗拒會標記自家產品問題的設備，仍可能未達目標 2.3（","Next measurement":"下一步量測","Interview at least one exporter or packing house; compare VOC-screening time with visual symptom onset; collect batch-level loss records and model whether shared access protects smallholder income.":"至少訪談一間出口商或包裝場；比較 VOC 篩檢時間與目視症狀出現時間；收集批次損失記錄，並建立模型檢視共用取得方式是否保護小農所得。","SDG 9 — Industry, Innovation & Infrastructure":"SDG 9——產業、創新與基礎設施","Shared stack":"共用架構","Target 9.5 — enhance research and industrial technological capability. Target 9.b — support domestic technology development.":"目標 9.5：增強研究與產業技術能力。目標 9.b：支持在地技術開發。","Sensing-element performance (selectivity, sensitivity, lifetime, reproducibility) is the hard constraint — not electronics or algorithms alone. Stakeholder record:":"感測元件效能（選擇性、靈敏度、壽命、重現性）才是主要限制，而不只是電子或演算法。利害關係人記錄：","Living":"活體","OR/Orco + GCaMP reporter cells as a swappable sensing element; team-designed ESP32-standalone four-channel FDM/DLIA reader; neuromorphic classification with a published research lineage through advisors. Portable architecture is intended — not field-validated.":"OR／Orco 加 GCaMP 報導細胞，作為可替換感測元件；團隊設計的 ESP32 獨立式四通道 FDM／DLIA 讀取器；以及透過顧問連結至已發表研究脈絡的神經形態分類。可攜式架構是設計意圖，尚未經現場驗證。","The advisors’ published mushroom-body research provides a lineage for the classifier, not a test of AeroSense’s agricultural accuracy.":"顧問已發表的蘑菇體研究提供分類器的研究脈絡，不是 AeroSense 農業準確率的測試。","P2 plate-reader pilot":"P2 微孔盤讀取器先導試驗","adds preliminary laboratory observations; it does not validate the complete cartridge-to-classifier system. Design and gap status:":"增加初步實驗室觀察，但不能驗證從匣體到分類器的完整系統。設計與缺口狀態：","Living cells add biosafety and consumable burden. IP that is only “planned / in preparation” could later restrict which buyers get access (see SDG 10 /":"活細胞增加生物安全與耗材負擔。目前仍「規劃／準備中」的智慧財產，未來可能限制哪些買方能取得（見 SDG 10／","). Extra-lab live-cell use remains restricted on the Safety page.":"）。安全頁面仍限制實驗室外的活細胞使用。","Complete component tests, lock-in readout, fluorescence-standard calibration, environmental-noise checks and live-cell end-to-end testing. Record measured power at each relevant stage and include culture, consumables and cold-chain requirements in the footprint boundary.":"完成元件測試、鎖相讀取、螢光標準品校正、環境雜訊檢查，以及活細胞端到端測試。記錄各相關階段的實測功耗，並將培養、耗材與冷鏈需求納入足跡邊界。","SDG 12 — Responsible Consumption & Production":"SDG 12——責任消費與生產","Tracks A + B":"路線 A＋B","12.3 food loss/waste; 12.5 waste reduction through reuse; 12.4 sound management of chemicals and wastes — including our own.":"12.3 食品損失／浪費；12.5 透過重用減少廢棄物；12.4 妥善管理化學品與廢棄物，也包含我們自己產生的部分。","Late spoilage detection can lead to batch rejection. Screening may also create unnecessary discard if false positives are acted on. The relevant comparison includes food decisions, sample preparation, reagents and consumables in each workflow.":"太晚發現腐敗可能造成整批退貨；若依偽陽性採取行動，篩檢也可能造成不必要丟棄。相關比較須納入各流程的食品決策、樣品前處理、試劑與耗材。","Designed as non-destructive headspace screening with modular cartridges intended for multiple readings before replacement, and risk-tier outputs rather than a binary discard signal. Recyclable or biodegradable housing and a simple LCA are planned — not completed.":"設計採用非破壞性頂空篩檢，搭配預期更換前可多次讀取的模組化匣體，以及風險分級輸出，而非二元丟棄訊號。可回收或生物可分解外殼與簡單生命週期評估，仍在規劃中，尚未完成。","Survey / design / gap status:":"問卷／設計／缺口狀態：","Living-cell cartridges are themselves consumables. “Self-renewing cells ⇒ lower replacement frequency” remains a hypothesis until lifetime and LCA exist (":"活細胞匣體本身也是耗材。在取得壽命與生命週期評估之前，「細胞可自我更新，所以更換頻率較低」仍是假說（","). We do not claim a net environmental benefit.":"）。我們不宣稱淨環境效益。","Verify the expanded survey and test risk-tier comprehension; measure usable cartridge lifetime; complete a wet-lab waste and hazard log; compare the full screening workflow with a defined confirmation workflow in a screening LCA.":"核實擴大後的問卷並測試風險分級理解；量測可用匣體壽命；完成濕實驗廢棄物與危害記錄；以初步生命週期評估，比較完整篩檢流程與明確定義的確認流程。","SDG 17 — Partnerships for the Goals":"SDG 17——促進目標實現的夥伴關係","Process":"過程","17.16 / 17.17 — multi-stakeholder knowledge sharing that changes what we build.":"17.16／17.17：能改變建構內容的多方利害關係人知識共享。","Without external correction, sustainability pages collapse into desk research and logo walls.":"沒有外部修正，永續頁面很容易只剩資料研究與標誌展示。","Field and industry knowledge-sharing, academic collaboration and FITI / NTHU Garage+ mentorship each contributed different expertise. The":"實地與產業知識共享、學術合作，以及 FITI／NTHU Garage+ 導師指導，各自貢獻不同專業。","engagement record":"接觸記錄","links those inputs to decisions.":"將這些意見連結至決策。","Engagement maturity status:":"接觸成熟度狀態：",". No contracted commercial partnership claimed; cross-team iGEM SDG collaboration not yet confirmed.":"。不宣稱已簽約的商業合作；跨 iGEM 團隊的 SDG 合作也尚未確認。","Completed interviews and shared research do not establish a commercial contract. A prepared visit to another domestic electronic-nose company remains prospective until it is conducted and its outputs are documented.":"完成訪談與共享研究，不等於建立商業合約。已準備的另一家國內電子鼻公司參訪，在實際進行並記錄產出之前，仍屬潛在接觸。","Conduct the prepared company visit and record its outcome; initiate at least one formal industry-partnership conversation; publish the scope and responsibilities of any resulting collaboration.":"執行已準備的公司參訪並記錄結果；至少啟動一場正式產業合作對話；公布由此形成合作的範圍與責任。","06 · Supporting":"06 · 支持性目標","Shorter pathways that surfaced in our own evidence, treated as supporting rather than primary.":"由自身證據浮現的較短路徑，列為支持性而非主要目標。","SDG 3 — Good Health & Well-being":"SDG 3——健康與福祉","Track B discipline":"路線 B 的紀律","Health-protective claim discipline for any food-adjacent screen.":"所有食品相關篩檢，都須維持保護健康的主張紀律。","A mold VOC is not automatically a food-safety or mycotoxin verdict. Stakeholder record:":"黴菌 VOC 不會自動成為食品安全或真菌毒素判定。利害關係人記錄：","Position AeroSense as rapid risk":"將 AeroSense 定位為快速風險","screening":"篩檢","that recommends confirmatory lab testing — never a diagnostic replacement. Risk-tier outputs are a design proposal; updated survey item counts are pending.":"，建議後續實驗室確認性檢測，絕非診斷替代品。風險分級輸出是設計提案；更新問卷逐題人數仍待取得。","Claim-discipline status:":"主張紀律狀態：","AeroSense does":"AeroSense 並","claim mycotoxin detection (":"宣稱可偵測真菌毒素（","). Overtrust of a “green” tier remains a safety failure mode.":"）。過度信任「綠燈」等級，仍是一種安全失敗模式。","Confirmatory-escalation UX tests; keep non-claims visible in operator materials.":"測試轉交確認流程的使用者體驗；在操作材料中清楚保留未提出的主張。","SDG 10 — Reduced Inequalities":"SDG 10——減少不平等","Access":"可近性","Avoid locking screening capability to only the best-resourced buyers.":"避免篩檢能力只限資源最充裕的買方取得。","Individual-farmer pricing can exclude smallholders and may face adoption resistance.":"以個別農民為對象的定價，可能排除小農，也可能面臨採用阻力。","Current design response: sell or pilot through associations, cooperatives, stations, and certification-adjacent bodies.":"目前的設計回應：透過協會／農會、合作社、改良場及認證相關機構銷售或試點。","Access / buyer status:":"可近性／買方狀態：",". Outcome equity is not validated.":"。結果公平性尚未驗證。","Intention is not an equitable outcome. Restrictive licensing later could recreate the same exclusion from the IP side.":"意圖不等於公平結果。未來限制性授權，可能從智慧財產端重現相同排除。","Pricing and distribution pilots that record who actually gets access.":"進行定價與配送試點，記錄究竟誰實際取得使用機會。","07 · Trade-offs":"07 · 取捨","SDGs do not operate independently on this project. Select a marked cell (desktop) or a card (all sizes) to read the relationship. Relationship detail text also appears in the panel below — readable without JavaScript. Empty cells mean we are not inventing a link — not that the goals are unrelated in the world.":"在本專案中，SDGs 不是各自獨立運作。選取標示的格子（桌機）或卡片（所有尺寸），閱讀關係說明。下方區塊也呈現關係詳情，不需 JavaScript 即可閱讀。空白格代表我們不捏造連結，而不是認為這些目標在現實世界無關。","Synergy":"相互促進","Tension":"矛盾","Unresolved":"尚未釐清","Symbols and words travel together. Color is optional emphasis only.":"符號與文字同時呈現，顏色只作輔助強調。","Pairwise relationships among SDGs 2, 3, 9, 10, 12, and 17":"SDG 2、3、9、10、12、17 之間的兩兩關係","From \\ To":"來源／對象","Same goal":"相同目標","Tension between SDG 2 and SDG 3":"SDG 2 與 SDG 3 的矛盾","Synergy between SDG 2 and SDG 9":"SDG 2 與 SDG 9 的相互促進","Tension between SDG 2 and SDG 10":"SDG 2 與 SDG 10 的矛盾","Tension between SDG 2 and SDG 12":"SDG 2 與 SDG 12 的矛盾","Unresolved between SDG 2 and SDG 17":"SDG 2 與 SDG 17 的關係尚未釐清","See SDG 2 × 3":"查看 SDG 2 × 3","No team-encoded link":"團隊未建立此連結","Tension between SDG 3 and SDG 12":"SDG 3 與 SDG 12 的矛盾","Synergy between SDG 3 and SDG 17":"SDG 3 與 SDG 17 的相互促進","See SDG 2 × 9":"查看 SDG 2 × 9","Tension between SDG 9 and SDG 10":"SDG 9 與 SDG 10 的矛盾","Tension between SDG 9 and SDG 12":"SDG 9 與 SDG 12 的矛盾","Synergy between SDG 9 and SDG 17":"SDG 9 與 SDG 17 的相互促進","See SDG 2 × 10":"查看 SDG 2 × 10","See SDG 9 × 10":"查看 SDG 9 × 10","Synergy between SDG 10 and SDG 17":"SDG 10 與 SDG 17 的相互促進","See SDG 2 × 12":"查看 SDG 2 × 12","See SDG 3 × 12":"查看 SDG 3 × 12","See SDG 9 × 12":"查看 SDG 9 × 12","Same goal · see also own-footprint tension in detail cards":"相同目標 · 另見詳情卡片中的自身足跡矛盾","Unresolved between SDG 12 and SDG 17":"SDG 12 與 SDG 17 的關係尚未釐清","See SDG 2 × 17":"查看 SDG 2 × 17","See SDG 3 × 17":"查看 SDG 3 × 17","See SDG 9 × 17":"查看 SDG 9 × 17","See SDG 10 × 17":"查看 SDG 10 × 17","See SDG 12 × 17":"查看 SDG 12 × 17","SDG 2 ↔ 12":"SDG 2 ↔ 12","Loss reduction vs unnecessary discard":"減少損失與不必要丟棄的取捨","SDG 3 ↔ 12":"SDG 3 ↔ 12","Waste avoidance vs false-negative harm":"避免浪費與偽陰性傷害的取捨","SDG 2 ↔ 10":"SDG 2 ↔ 10","Exporter resilience vs smallholder access":"出口商韌性與小農取得機會的取捨","SDG 9 ↔ 10":"SDG 9 ↔ 10","IP / commercialization vs unequal access":"智慧財產／商業化與取得機會不平等","SDG 9 ↔ 12":"SDG 9 ↔ 12","Living-cell innovation vs own waste":"活細胞創新與自身廢棄物","SDG 2 ↔ 3":"SDG 2 ↔ 3","Keep shipping pressure off diagnostic claims":"避免出貨壓力影響診斷主張","SDG 2 ↔ 9":"SDG 2 ↔ 9","Agri screening aims need sensing innovation":"農業篩檢目標需要感測創新","SDG 3 ↔ 17":"SDG 3 ↔ 17","Biotech engagement hardened claim discipline":"生技產業接觸強化主張紀律","SDG 9 ↔ 17":"SDG 9 ↔ 17","E-nose CSO engagement shaped sensing bet":"電子鼻 CSO 接觸塑造感測方向","SDG 10 ↔ 17":"SDG 10 ↔ 17","Analytical engagement corrected buyer segment":"分析儀器接觸修正買方區隔","SDG 2 ↔ 17":"SDG 2 ↔ 17","Field input ≠ exporter partnership":"實地意見不等於出口商合作","SDG 12 ↔ 17":"SDG 12 ↔ 17","No co-owned LCA yet":"尚無共同負責的生命週期評估","· SDG 2 ↔ SDG 12":"· SDG 2 ↔ SDG 12","Earlier VOC screening":"較早的 VOC 篩檢","aims":"旨在","to reduce supply-chain food loss (2) and over-caution waste (12). The same decision layer can also cause unnecessary discard via false positives, while living-cell cartridges create waste of their own. Net food-system benefit is not measured.":"減少供應鏈食品損失（2）與過度謹慎造成的浪費（12）。但同一決策層也可能透過偽陽性造成不必要丟棄，而活細胞匣體本身會產生廢棄物。食品系統的淨效益尚未量測。","Evidence status:":"證據狀態：","on loss/waste reduction · cartridge LCA":"：減少損失／浪費 · 匣體生命週期評估","SDG 2 pathway":"SDG 2 路徑","SDG 12 pathway":"SDG 12 路徑","Own footprint":"自身足跡","· SDG 3 ↔ SDG 12":"· SDG 3 ↔ SDG 12","Avoiding unnecessary disposal must not come at the cost of unsafe false negatives. Claim boundary:":"避免不必要丟棄，不能以不安全的偽陰性為代價。主張範圍：","survey item analysis ·":"問卷逐題分析 ·","claim boundary · outcome":"主張範圍 · 結果","· SDG 2 ↔ SDG 10":"· SDG 2 ↔ SDG 10","A Target 2.4-style resilience win for exporters can fail Target 2.3 / SDG 10 if smallholders never receive protection — or if they resist tools that flag their own product.":"即使出口商獲得符合目標 2.4 的韌性效益，若小農始終未受保護，或抗拒會標記自家產品問題的工具，仍可能未達目標 2.3／SDG 10。","farmer WTP resistance · equitable outcome":"農民付費意願阻力 · 公平結果","Who benefits":"誰受益","· SDG 9 ↔ SDG 10":"· SDG 9 ↔ SDG 10","Innovation and planned IP can support commercial defensibility (9) while restrictive licensing or pricing could limit which buyers — large exporters vs smallholder-serving associations — get access (10).":"創新與規劃中的智慧財產可支持商業防禦性（9），但限制性授權或定價，也可能影響哪些買方能取得使用機會（10）：大型出口商，還是服務小農的組織。","patents planned / novelty search not commissioned ·":"專利規劃中／尚未委託新穎性檢索 ·","Entrepreneurship · Risks":"創業 · 風險","· SDG 9 ↔ SDG 12":"· SDG 9 ↔ SDG 12","The living-cell sensing bet that answers industry selectivity limits also creates culture media, plastics, and cartridge waste. “Self-renewing ⇒ lower replacement” remains a hypothesis until lifetime and LCA exist.":"回應產業選擇性限制的活細胞感測方向，也會產生培養基、塑膠與匣體廢棄物。在取得壽命與生命週期評估之前，「自我更新所以較少更換」仍是假說。","architecture · net benefit":"架構 · 淨效益","· SDG 2 ↔ SDG 3":"· SDG 2 ↔ SDG 3","Pressure to keep produce moving (2) must not collapse into food-safety certification language (3). Screening recommends confirmatory testing; it does not detect mycotoxins.":"讓農產品持續流通的壓力（2），不能變成食品安全認證用語（3）。篩檢建議確認性檢測，並不偵測真菌毒素。","boundary":"範圍","· SDG 2 ↔ SDG 9":"· SDG 2 ↔ SDG 9","Agricultural early-warning aims depend on a sensing-element advance that conventional e-nose interviews themselves describe as the bottleneck. Synergy is intended — field performance is not shown.":"農業早期預警目標，依賴感測元件的進展；傳統電子鼻訪談本身也將它指出為瓶頸。相互促進是意圖，現場效能尚未展示。","outcome ·":"結果 ·","stack":"架構","· SDG 3 ↔ SDG 17":"· SDG 3 ↔ SDG 17","Biotechnology-industry engagement directly improved health-protective claim discipline. That is knowledge-sharing synergy — not a formal commercial partnership.":"生技產業接觸直接改善了保護健康的主張紀律。這是知識共享的相互促進，不是正式商業合作。","engagement":"接觸","Who changed · Biotech":"誰帶來改變 · 生技","· SDG 9 ↔ SDG 17":"· SDG 9 ↔ SDG 17","Electronic-nose industry engagement redirected innovation effort toward the sensing element. Synergy of critique — still an engagement, not a formal partnership; prospective company visit remains unconducted.":"電子鼻產業接觸，將創新工作重新導向感測元件。這是批判意見帶來的相互促進，仍屬接觸而非正式合作；預定公司參訪尚未進行。","Who changed · E-nose":"誰帶來改變 · 電子鼻","· SDG 10 ↔ SDG 17":"· SDG 10 ↔ SDG 17","Analytical-instrumentation engagement corrected the buyer segment toward associations and certifiers — a design response to inequality risk. Equity outcomes remain unvalidated.":"分析儀器接觸將買方區隔修正為協會／農會與認證單位，是設計對不平等風險的回應。公平結果仍未驗證。","· outcome":"· 結果","Who changed · Analytical":"誰帶來改變 · 分析儀器","· SDG 2 ↔ SDG 17":"· SDG 2 ↔ SDG 17","Agricultural-station and association engagements shaped the beachhead story, but exporter/packing-house interviews are still missing. Stakeholder collaboration can improve decisions; interview ≠ partnership; partnership maturity for the actual payer is unresolved.":"農業改良場與協會／農會的接觸塑造灘頭堡故事，但出口商／包裝場訪談仍然缺少。利害關係人合作可改善決策，但訪談不等於夥伴關係；與真正付費者的合作成熟度仍未釐清。","upstream · payer":"上游 · 付費者","· SDG 12 ↔ SDG 17":"· SDG 12 ↔ SDG 17","No co-owned life-cycle assessment or waste audit partnership exists yet. Until that work is done with clear methods, SDG 12 claims stay internal hypotheses.":"尚未建立共同負責的生命週期評估或廢棄物稽核合作。在以清楚方法完成此工作之前，SDG 12 主張仍是內部假說。","Next measurements":"下一步量測","08 · Evidence boundary":"08 · 證據範圍","This ledger is the honest boundary of the Sustainability page. Status labels are not decoration: a hypothesis must not look like a measurement. Limitations stay visible — they are not tucked into a closed accordion.":"這份清單如實界定永續頁面的證據範圍。狀態標籤不是裝飾：假說不能看起來像量測。限制持續可見，不藏在收合區塊裡。","Claim language guide":"主張用語指南","Measured":"已量測","→ “we observed / measured”":"→「我們觀察到／量測到」","→ “stakeholders told us / interviews reshaped”":"→「利害關係人告訴我們／訪談重新塑造」","→ “we estimate”":"→「我們估計」","→ “we designed”":"→「我們設計了」","→ “could / may / we hypothesize”":"→「可能／或許／我們假設」","→ “we do not yet know”":"→「我們尚不知道」","Filter ledger":"篩選清單","Open gap":"待補證據","Showing all entries":"顯示所有項目","Filters require JavaScript. Without it, every entry below remains fully readable.":"篩選需要 JavaScript；未啟用時，下方所有項目仍完整可讀。","Public survey reanalysis (n = 107 team reported)":"大眾問卷重新分析（團隊回報 n = 107）","Pending analysis":"等待分析","Evidence / source":"證據／來源","Team public survey, 2026-08-23. Updated item-level counts have not been supplied. See":"團隊大眾問卷，2026-08-23。未提供更新的逐題人數。詳見","Education · Public survey":"教育 · 大眾問卷","for the instrument and verification status.":"，了解工具與核實狀態。","Allows us to say":"可允許的說法","The early n = 28 aggregate findings are published on Education. A later total of 107 is team reported, but no updated item-level table is supplied. The two stages cannot be used interchangeably.":"早期 n = 28 彙整結果已公布於教育頁面。後期總數 107 是團隊回報，但未提供更新逐題表格。兩階段不能互換使用。","Does":"並","allow us to say":"允許我們宣稱","Population prevalence for Taiwan; that Education interventions caused learning gain; that consumers are paying customers.":"臺灣人口的盛行比例、教育介入造成學習增益，或消費者是付費客戶。","Relevant SDG":"相關 SDG","3, 12 (claim discipline / over-caution context)":"3、12（主張紀律／過度謹慎的背景）","Paired pre/post learning evaluation when workshop cohorts exist.":"待工作坊群體形成後，進行配對前後測學習評估。","Discard-behavior rate claimed in earlier drafts":"早期草稿宣稱的丟棄行為比例","Appears in some team syntheses (IHP / Entrepreneurship drafts).":"出現在部分團隊整理內容中（IHP／創業草稿）。","Not":"並未","currently tabulated on the Education survey tables.":"列入目前教育頁面的問卷表格。","Nothing publishable as a measured count until the instrument matches Education.":"在工具與教育頁面一致前，沒有可作為實測人數發布的內容。","We measured a specific discard behavior rate.":"我們量測了某個特定丟棄行為比例。","The raw item and codebook have not been supplied. We do not use the “100% discard” claim to calculate avoided waste or justify a population-level conclusion.":"尚未提供原始題目與編碼手冊。我們不使用「100% 丟棄」主張計算避免的浪費，或支持人口層級結論。","Beachhead problem sizing (Taiwan banana fungal-disease desk estimate)":"灘頭堡問題規模估算（臺灣香蕉真菌病害資料研究估計）","The Sustainability draft estimates NT$3.51 billion per year from 33.6% of NT$10.445 billion sector output. This is team problem-sizing context; the scope and underlying statistics need a traceable primary source. See":"永續草稿以產業產值新臺幣 104.45 億元的 33.6%，估計每年新臺幣 35.1 億元。這是團隊問題規模的背景；範圍與基礎統計仍需可追溯的第一手來源。詳見","The team used a sector-level estimate to motivate export-chain interviews. It is not a measured shipment loss or recoverable saving.":"團隊使用產業層級估計，作為進行出口鏈訪談的動機。它不是實測貨運損失，也不是可回收的節省金額。","That AeroSense has prevented that loss, or that the figure is an audited national statistic published on Sustainability.":"AeroSense 已避免這些損失，或此數字是永續頁面公布的經稽核國家統計。","Exporter-side loss volumes; attach primary statistical source on Entrepreneurship before treating as a public fact.":"出口商端損失量；在當作公開事實前，先於創業頁面附上第一手統計來源。","Field and industry engagements reshaped beachhead, buyer, and claim boundaries":"實地與產業接觸重新塑造灘頭堡市場、買方與主張範圍","Stakeholder evidence is documented in":"利害關係人證據記錄於","Taoyuan":"桃園","associations / farms":"協會／農會與農場","e-nose CSO":"電子鼻 CSO","Challenge Bioproducts":"Challenge Bioproducts","analytical instrumentation":"分析儀器","advisors":"顧問","). Commercial consequence:":"）。商業影響：",". This card records the SDG consequence of those engagements.":"。此卡片記錄這些接觸對 SDG 的影響。","SDG-facing consequences of those Human Practices decisions:":"這些人文實踐決策對 SDG 的影響：","Shared institutional screening (associations / stations / cooperatives / certifiers) rather than individual-farmer purchase — SDG 2.3 / SDG 10 access tension.":"採機構共用篩檢（協會／農會、改良場、合作社、認證單位），而非個別農民購買，對應 SDG 2.3／SDG 10 的取得機會矛盾。","Screening-not-diagnostic / VOC ≠ mycotoxin boundary — SDG 3 claim discipline.":"篩檢而非診斷，且 VOC 不等於真菌毒素的範圍，對應 SDG 3 主張紀律。","Innovation bet on the living sensing element rather than electronics-alone — SDG 9 pathway (field performance not shown).":"將創新方向放在活體感測元件，而非只靠電子技術，對應 SDG 9 路徑（尚未展示現場效能）。","Device pilots occurred; formal commercial partnerships exist; quotes are verbatim without transcript verification.":"已進行設備試點、存在正式商業合作，或在未核實逐字稿時宣稱引用為原話。","Publish consented IHP engagement cards; exporter/packing-house interviews.":"公布經同意的 IHP 接觸卡片；訪談出口商／包裝場。","Individual farmers often show low willingness to pay / may resist tools that flag their own product":"個別農民常有較低付費意願，或可能抗拒會標記自家產品問題的工具","Human Practices · buyers":"人文實踐· 買方",". Reinforced that associations are more plausible buyers than individual farmers.":"。這強化了協會／農會比個別農民更可能成為買方的方向。","Interview-derived adoption concern pushed buyer design toward associations / stations / cooperatives / certifiers.":"訪談衍生的採用疑慮，使買方設計轉向協會／農會、改良場、合作社與認證單位。","A census of Taiwanese farmers; that association buyers have been contracted.":"臺灣農民普查結果，或協會／農會買方已簽約。","Association buyer willingness-to-pay and access pilots.":"機構買方付費意願與取得機會試點。","ESP32-standalone current design reader architecture (Raspberry Pi removed)":"目前設計的 ESP32 獨立式讀取器架構（已移除 Raspberry Pi）","September 2026 documentation; current design layout dated 11 Sept 2026; KiCad renders in-repo.":"2026 年 9 月文件；目前設計佈局日期為 2026 年 9 月 11 日；儲存庫中有 KiCad 繪圖。","We designed an ESP32-centered portable reader architecture; Pi is a retired iteration.":"我們設計了以 ESP32 為核心的可攜式讀取器架構；Pi 是已淘汰的迭代。","Measured optical/electrical performance, battery life, or “under 1 W” operation.":"實測光學／電氣效能、電池續航，或「低於 1 W」運作。","Hardware validation ladder after fabrication.":"製造後的硬體驗證階梯。","Risk-tier screening output (not binary discard / not silent “safe”)":"風險分級篩檢輸出（不是二元丟棄，也不是無說明的「安全」）","Product framing on Entrepreneurship / Description and":"創業／專案介紹的產品定位，以及","Human Practices · claim boundary":"人文實踐· 主張範圍",". Survey item-level support remains unverified.":"。問卷逐題支持仍未核實。","We designed the communication layer as risk tiers with confirmatory escalation.":"我們將溝通層設計為風險分級，搭配轉交確認的升級流程。","That the UI exists in the field or that tiers reduce waste or harm.":"介面已在現場使用，或分級減少了浪費與傷害。","Operator UX tests for escalation behavior.":"對升級處理行為進行操作人員使用者體驗測試。","Non-destructive headspace cartridge intended for multiple readings before replacement":"非破壞性頂空匣體，預期更換前可多次讀取","Product / Parts architecture; Entrepreneurship “intended non-destructive — not validated in field.”":"產品／元件架構；創業頁面：「預期為非破壞性，尚未經現場驗證」。","We designed for non-destructive screening and modular cartridges.":"我們以非破壞性篩檢與模組化匣體為設計目標。","Validated reuse cycles, lifetime advantage, or sealed field cartridges.":"已驗證的重用次數、壽命優勢，或密封場域匣體。","Reuse-cycle protocol with n; containment validation under Safety constraints.":"具有 n 的重用循環流程；在安全限制下進行封存驗證。","AeroSense reduces food loss or food waste in practice":"AeroSense 在實務上減少食品損失或浪費","None measured. Causal pathway hypothesized on SDG 2 / 12 sections.":"尚無量測。SDG 2／12 章節僅提出因果路徑假說。","We hypothesize / it could / it may support earlier triage decisions that reduce loss — if validated later.":"我們假設它可能支持更早的分流決策，進而減少損失，前提是後續完成驗證。","“AeroSense reduces / prevents / has reduced food waste.”":"「AeroSense 減少／防止／已減少食品浪費。」","Field or packing-house pilots with before/after loss metrics.":"具有前後損失指標的場域或包裝場試點。","Self-renewing living cells yield lower replacement frequency than conventional e-nose sensors":"可自我更新的活細胞，比傳統電子鼻感測器需要更低的更換頻率","Mechanistic design rationale; industry lifetime pain paraphrased from CSO engagement (context-specific). “Near-daily replacement” for some commercial sensors is industry paraphrase (context-specific), not a universal e-nose fact.":"機制性設計依據；使用壽命痛點由 CSO 接觸內容轉述，限特定情境。部分商用感測器「幾乎每天更換」也是情境限定的產業轉述，不是所有電子鼻的普遍事實。","We hypothesize a lifetime advantage; industry flags lifetime as a pain point for some products.":"我們假設存在壽命優勢；產業指出部分產品的使用壽命是痛點。","Measured cartridge lifetime, “near-daily” as a universal e-nose fact, or net environmental benefit.":"實測匣體壽命、把「幾乎每天」當成所有電子鼻的普遍事實，或淨環境效益。","Lifetime / drift protocols; LCA comparing replacement schedules.":"壽命／漂移流程；比較更換時程的生命週期評估。","Fungal / disease VOC signatures are detectable and actionable with the current receptor set":"目前受體組合可偵測真菌／病害 VOC 特徵，且足以支持行動","Beachhead hypothesis; Parts / Zboray-oriented library lineage — no field VOC performance published.":"灘頭堡假說；元件／以 Zboray 為基礎的受體庫脈絡，尚無已公布的現場 VOC 效能。","We hypothesize detectability for beachhead-relevant VOCs; wet-lab and field proof are still required.":"我們假設灘頭堡相關 VOC 可被偵測；仍需要濕實驗與現場證據。","Field diagnostic capability, accuracy, detection limits, or disease diagnosis.":"現場診斷能力、準確率、偵測極限或病害診斷。","Labeled receptor responses under controlled then field-relevant conditions.":"先在受控條件，再於貼近現場的條件下，取得附標籤的受體反應。","Lower environmental footprint / net LCA benefit vs destructive assays or conventional sensors":"相較破壞性試驗或傳統感測器，有較低環境足跡／淨生命週期效益","None. Explicitly not completed on Sustainability draft and Entrepreneurship responsible-scaling notes.":"無。永續草稿與創業負責任擴展筆記都明確表示尚未完成。","We do not yet know net footprint.":"我們尚不知道淨足跡。","“Greener,” “lower footprint,” or “recyclable housing delivered.”":"「更環保」、「足跡較低」或「已交付可回收外殼」。","Simple LCA + wet-lab plastics / hazard-class inventory.":"簡單生命週期評估，加上濕實驗塑膠／危害類別清單。","Reader power consumption (including any “under 1 W” claim)":"讀取器功耗（包含任何「低於 1 W」主張）","The Sustainability draft names a below-1 W design aspiration. Current Hardware uses an ESP32-standalone reader; no measured power result is supplied.":"永續草稿提出低於 1 W 的設計願景。目前硬體採 ESP32 獨立式讀取器，但未提供實測功耗結果。","We do not yet know operating power.":"我們尚不知道操作功耗。","Any wattage figure as measured performance.":"將任何瓦數當作實測效能。","Bench power after electrical bring-up.":"電氣啟用測試後，量測工作臺功耗。","Field diagnostic / field-ready screening capability":"現場診斷／可直接現場使用的篩檢能力","Hardware validation ladder pending; Safety restricts extra-lab live-cell use; no device pilot claimed.":"硬體驗證階梯待完成；安全要求限制實驗室外的活細胞使用；未宣稱已進行設備試點。","Field diagnostic capability is":"現場診斷能力","not established":"尚未建立","“Field-deployable,” “ready for packing houses,” or “validated on bananas in Taiwan.”":"「可現場部署」、「已可供包裝場使用」或「已在臺灣香蕉上驗證」。","Lab evidence first, then consented pilots with site SOP.":"先取得實驗室證據，再依場域標準作業程序進行經同意的試點。","Mycotoxin / aflatoxin detection or food-safety certification":"真菌毒素／黃麴毒素偵測，或食品安全認證","Explicit non-claim from":"明確未提出的主張，來自","Human Practices · Challenge Bioproducts":"人文實踐· Challenge Bioproducts","and Safety boundary.":"與安全範圍。","We do not claim mycotoxin detection; VOC ≠ toxin verdict.":"我們不宣稱可偵測真菌毒素；VOC 不等於毒素判定。","Any diagnostic or certificate language.":"任何診斷或認證用語。","Keep confirmatory escalation in operator materials; no toxin assay roadmap claimed here.":"在操作材料保留轉交確認流程；此處不宣稱有毒素檢測開發路線。","Patent filings completed / freedom-to-operate established":"已完成專利申請／已確立自由實施空間","Entrepreneurship: novelty search not commissioned; provisional filings planned, not filed.":"創業頁面：尚未委託新穎性檢索；臨時專利申請規劃中，尚未提出。","We do not yet know IP posture beyond “planned.”":"除了「規劃中」，我們尚不清楚智慧財產狀態。","“Patents filed” or “FTO cleared.”":"「已申請專利」或「已通過 FTO」。","Commission novelty/FTO search; document filing dates if/when they exist.":"委託新穎性／自由實施（FTO）檢索；若實際申請，再記錄日期。","Exporter / packing-house buyer validation":"出口商／包裝場買方驗證","Documented gap on Entrepreneurship / Engineering (“would do differently”). No banana/mango exporter interview on record.":"創業／工程頁面（「如果重來會怎麼做」）記錄的缺口。沒有香蕉／芒果出口商訪談記錄。","We do not yet know payer economics from the actual beachhead buyer.":"我們尚不清楚真正灘頭堡買方的付費經濟條件。","First customer, LOI, or packing-house pilot outcomes.":"第一位客戶、意向書或包裝場試點成果。","Direct exporter / packing-house interviews with dated notes.":"直接訪談出口商／包裝場，並留下具日期的筆記。","The functional unit is":"功能單位為","one tonne of a defined food lot screened through a stated storage and decision interval":"在明確的儲存與決策期間內，對一公噸已定義食品批次進行篩檢",", compared with the same lot under the existing workflow. No avoided-food-loss or carbon result has been measured. This model makes the required measurements explicit instead of assigning a benefit to an SDG label.":"，並與相同批次在既有流程下的結果比較。尚未量測避免的食品損失或碳排結果。此模型明確列出所需量測，而不是直接替 SDG 標籤賦予效益。","Definitions, units and required inputs for estimating retained food mass, net emissions and operating value per tonne screened. Sensitivity ranges are mathematical bounds; no current measured net benefit or carbon break-even value is asserted.":"估計每公噸篩檢所保留食品質量、淨排放與操作價值的定義、單位與必要輸入。敏感度範圍是數學邊界；不宣稱目前已有實測淨效益或碳損益平衡值。","Quantity":"量","Definition / equation":"定義／方程式","Input evidence and sensitivity":"輸入證據與敏感度","Food retained ΔM (kg / tonne screened)":"保留食品 ΔM（kg／每公噸篩檢）","Baseline discarded mass − screened-workflow discarded mass":"基準流程丟棄質量－篩檢流程丟棄質量","Matched lots and follow-up outcomes needed. Count unnecessary discard from false positives; no current measured value.":"需要相符批次與後續結果；須計入偽陽性造成的不必要丟棄，目前無實測值。","Net emissions ΔE (kg CO₂e / tonne)":"淨排放 ΔE（kg CO₂e／公噸）","ΔM × food emission factor − added device, cartridge, energy and disposal burden":"ΔM × 食品排放係數－新增的設備、匣體、能源與處置負擔","Food-, location- and system-boundary-specific factor required. No default factor is assigned. A negative result means added emissions.":"需要符合食品、地點與系統邊界的係數，不設定預設係數。負值表示排放增加。","Net operating value ΔC (NTD / tonne)":"淨操作價值 ΔC（NTD／公噸）","ΔM × recoverable unit value − testing, confirmation, labor, handling and disposal costs":"ΔM × 可回收單位價值－檢測、確認、人工、處理與處置成本","Recoverable value is not retail price by default. No shipment ledger or verified test-cost input exists.":"可回收價值不預設等於零售價。目前無出貨帳冊或已核實的檢測成本輸入。","Sensitivity to action":"對行動的敏感度","Vary avoided-loss fraction and additional-discard fraction over 0–1":"將避免損失比例與額外丟棄比例，在 0–1 之間調整","These are mathematical bounds, not observed rates. Their combination must remain consistent with the lot’s actual loss and rejection fractions.":"這些是數學邊界，不是觀察比例；兩者組合必須符合該批次實際損失與拒收比例。","Carbon break-even (kg retained / tonne)":"碳損益平衡（kg 保留量／公噸）","Additional system burden ÷ food emission factor, when factor > 0":"當食品排放係數 > 0 時，額外系統負擔 ÷ 食品排放係數","A decision threshold only; not calculated until both inputs are traceable.":"僅為決策門檻；兩個輸入都可追溯之前，不予計算。","Safety constraint":"安全限制","Food retained cannot be counted as a benefit if it introduces an unacceptable safety outcome":"若保留食品帶來不可接受的安全結果，就不能算作效益","Confirmatory workflow and false-negative outcomes remain separate from mass and carbon accounting.":"確認流程與偽陰性結果，仍須與質量及碳排核算分開。","The model cannot turn a VOC alert into evidence that food is safe. A pilot must compare the decisions and outcomes produced by the two workflows, not simply multiply a claimed detection rate by national food losses.":"此模型不能將 VOC 警示變成食品安全證據。試點必須比較兩種流程產生的決策與結果，不能只把宣稱的檢出率乘上全國食品損失。","Download the input and equation template (CSV)":"下載輸入與方程式範本（CSV）","Life-cycle inventory: reader plus recurring biology":"生命週期清單：讀取器加上持續的生物流程","Inventory boundary for a future comparative assessment":"未來比較評估的盤查邊界","Available record":"現有記錄","Measurement needed":"所需量測","Reader production":"讀取器生產","BOM and CAD":"物料清單與 CAD","specify components":"列明元件","Mass and materials, manufacturing routes, service lifetime, repairs and end-of-life":"質量與材料、製造途徑、使用壽命、維修與生命終期","Cartridge and cell culture":"匣體與細胞培養","Contained-use design and biological protocol":"封閉使用設計與生物實驗流程","Culture-media and consumable quantities, cartridge lifetime, replacement frequency and waste inactivation":"培養基與耗材用量、匣體壽命、更換頻率，以及廢棄物去活化","Use and confirmation":"使用與確認","Readout architecture and screening workflow":"讀取架構與篩檢流程","Energy per valid test, utilization, rejected runs, confirmatory tests, handling and transport":"每次有效檢測的能源、使用率、無效執行、確認性檢測、處理與運輸","Allocation":"分攤","Reader manufacture divided over its lifetime valid tests":"將讀取器製造負擔分攤至全壽命的有效檢測次數","Valid-test lifetime must be measured; a purchase price is not an emissions factor":"有效檢測壽命必須量測；購買價格不是排放係數","Shared research equipment and one-off development work should be reported separately from routine operation. Results must state whether avoided food-production burdens, transport, storage and disposal are inside the comparison. We have no completed LCA and make no carbon-reduction claim.":"共享研究設備與一次性開發工作，應與日常操作分開報告。結果必須說明比較是否包含避免的食品生產負擔、運輸、儲存與處置。我們尚未完成生命週期評估，也不提出減碳主張。","09 · Footprint":"09 · 足跡","Before claiming we reduce other people’s waste, we account for what AeroSense itself consumes. This is a system-boundary inventory —":"在宣稱減少他人的廢棄物之前，我們先盤點 AeroSense 自身消耗什麼。這是一份系統邊界清單，並","a completed life-cycle assessment. Where mass, energy, or hazard tallies do not exist, we write":"是已完成的生命週期評估。尚無質量、能源或危害統計的地方，我們寫","Not yet quantified":"尚未量化",", not zeros.":"，而不是填零。","No formal LCA has been completed for AeroSense. We do not claim a net environmental benefit.":"AeroSense 尚未完成正式生命週期評估；我們不宣稱淨環境效益。","Simple system boundary":"簡單系統邊界","Status labels mark what is designed or known in kind versus what is quantified. Quantified = a published measurement exists. Not yet quantified = known stream, no number on this wiki.":"狀態標籤區分「已設計或已知類別」與「已量化」。已量化＝已有公開量測；尚未量化＝已知存在的流量，但此 網站 沒有數字。","Flow: Inputs → AeroSense process → Outputs":"流程：輸入 → AeroSense 過程 → 輸出","Inputs":"輸入","Living-cell culture / media":"活細胞培養／培養液","HEK293 OR/Orco + reporter culture; media and biosafety handling required for the biological sensing layer.":"HEK293 OR／Orco 加報導蛋白培養；生物感測層需要培養基與生物安全處理。","Plastics / consumables":"塑膠／耗材","Wet-lab plastics and disposables generated during construct development and testing.":"構築開發與測試過程產生的濕實驗塑膠與拋棄式用品。","Sensing cartridge materials":"感測匣材料","Modular headspace cartridge architecture intended; material mass and housing polymer not selected / not weighed.":"預定採模組化頂空匣體架構；尚未選定／秤量材料質量與外殼聚合物。","Electronics":"電子元件","ESP32-standalone current design reader layout and portable power path on":"ESP32 獨立式目前讀取器佈局與可攜式供電路徑，見","; BOM mass and e-waste not tallied.":"；尚未統計物料質量與電子廢棄物。","Electricity":"電力","Reader power draw and lab equipment energy not measured. See":"尚未量測讀取器耗電與實驗室設備能源。詳見","Storage / transport requirements":"儲存／運輸需求","Biological layer likely needs culture / cold-chain conditions metal-oxide sensors do not — magnitude unknown.":"生物層可能需要金屬氧化物感測器所不需的培養／冷鏈條件，程度未知。","AeroSense process":"AeroSense 過程","Sensing":"感測","Non-destructive headspace VOC interaction with living-cell receptor arrays — field performance not established.":"頂空 VOC 與活細胞受體陣列的非破壞性交互作用；現場效能尚未建立。","Optical / fluorescence path on the ESP32-centered reader; validation ladder pending fabrication.":"以 ESP32 為核心的讀取器光學／螢光路徑；驗證階梯等待製造後進行。","Computation":"運算","Edge-capable pattern recognition intended; compute energy not measured.":"預期可在邊緣端進行模式辨識；運算能源尚未量測。","Cleaning / maintenance":"清潔／維護","Reuse and cleaning cycles for cartridges / fixtures not protocolled under Safety constraints yet.":"尚未在安全限制下制定匣體／固定裝置的重用與清潔循環流程。","Outputs":"輸出","Biological waste":"生物廢棄物","Culture waste and inactivated biological material under institutional biosafety rules — mass not logged here.":"依機構生物安全規範處理的培養廢棄物與去活化生物材料；此處未記錄質量。","Plastic waste":"塑膠廢棄物","Tips, tubes, plates, and eventual cartridge plastics — no published wet-lab plastic mass.":"吸頭、試管、培養盤與未來匣體塑膠；尚未公布濕實驗塑膠質量。","Electronic waste":"電子廢棄物","Reader boards, batteries, and failed prototypes — end-of-life pathway not selected.":"讀取器電路板、電池與失敗原型；尚未選定生命終期處理途徑。","Cartridge disposal":"感測匣廢棄處理","Intended multi-read cartridge then replacement; usable lifetime unvalidated. See":"預期一個匣體可多次讀取後再更換；可用壽命尚未驗證。詳見","Data / decision information":"資料／決策資訊","Intended output":"預期輸出","Risk-tier screening signal for human decision — not a confirmatory diagnostic. See":"供人員決策的風險分級篩檢訊號，不是確認性診斷。詳見","Before wiki freeze, measure these":"網站 定稿前，量測這些項目","Checklist for the team — empty boxes mean the measurement is still owed, not “zero impact.”":"團隊檢核表：空白方格代表仍欠缺量測，不是「零影響」。","Wet-lab plastic mass":"濕實驗塑膠質量","Relevant hazardous reagent categories":"相關危險試劑類別","Cartridge material mass":"匣體材料質量","Cartridge usable lifetime":"匣體可用壽命","Reader power draw":"讀取器耗電","Storage / cold-chain requirements":"儲存／冷鏈需求","Cleaning / reuse cycle":"清潔／重用循環","End-of-life pathway":"生命終期處理途徑","10 · Equity":"10 · 公平性","Potential benefits and exclusion risks for each stakeholder group. The final column distinguishes existing stakeholder input, hypotheses and validation that remains future work.":"各利害關係人群體的潛在效益與排除風險。最後一欄區分既有利害關係人意見、假說，以及仍屬未來工作的驗證。","Actor":"行動者","Potential benefit (hypothesis)":"潛在效益（假說）","Exclusion / burden risk":"排除／負擔風險","Exporters / packing houses":"出口商／包裝場","Earlier triage before visible spread":"在可見擴散前更早分流","May capture value alone; not yet interviewed":"可能獨占價值；尚未訪談","Associations / stations / cooperatives":"協會／農會、改良場、合作社","Shared screening capacity":"共用篩檢能力","Cost and capacity still unknown":"成本與能力仍未知","buyer shift":"買方轉移","Smallholders":"小農","Income protection":"所得保護","value flows down":"價值向下游分配至小農","Fear of being flagged; cannot buy alone":"害怕被標記；無法獨立購買","Confirmatory labs":"確認實驗室","Upstream screening feed":"上游篩檢轉介","Must remain in the loop — not “replaced”":"必須保留在流程中，不是被「取代」","Public / consumers (Track B)":"大眾／消費者（路線 B）","Less blind discard":"減少盲目丟棄","tool is trustworthy":"工具值得信任","Overtrust / false-negative harm":"過度信任／偽陰性傷害","updated survey analysis":"更新問卷分析","Future iGEM teams":"未來 iGEM 團隊","Reusable trade-off method":"可重用的取捨分析方法","This page":"本頁","11 · Reuse":"11 · 重用","This page should remain useful after 2026. Below is a reusable evidence framework future iGEM teams can copy — not a finished impact certificate for AeroSense.":"我們希望本頁在 2026 年之後仍有用。下方是未來 iGEM 團隊可複製的證據架構，不是 AeroSense 已完成的影響認證。","AeroSense Sustainability Evidence Canvas":"AeroSense 永續證據畫布","Ten fields force a team to name the stakeholder, the mechanism, both pathways, and the measurement still owed. Empty evidence cells stay empty. Status vocabulary matches this page: Measured · Stakeholder-backed · Estimated · Designed · Hypothesis · Open gap.":"十個欄位要求團隊明確寫出利害關係人、機制、正負兩條路徑，以及仍欠缺的量測。證據空格保持空白。狀態用語與本頁一致：已量測 · 利害關係人支持 · 估計 · 已設計 · 假說 · 待補缺口。","Filled example — AeroSense (banana screening beachhead)":"填寫範例：AeroSense（香蕉篩檢灘頭堡市場）","Illustrative row for one primary pathway. Not a claim of completed impact.":"一條主要路徑的示範列，不代表影響已完成。","SDG target":"SDG 細項目標","SDG 2.3 / 2.4 — reduce post-harvest loss risk for export banana value chains (Taiwan beachhead hypothesis)":"SDG 2.3／2.4：降低香蕉出口價值鏈的採後損失風險（臺灣灘頭堡假說）","Stakeholder":"利害關係人","Exporters / packing houses (intended buyer); associations / stations / cooperatives (access channel); smallholders (indirect)":"出口商／包裝場（預定買方）；協會／農會、改良場、合作社（取得管道）；小農（間接）","Problem observed":"觀察到的問題","Fungal disease risk is hard to triage early; desk estimate frames large at-risk sector value; packing-house loss volumes still an open gap":"真菌病害風險難以提早分流；資料研究估計指出大量產業價值可能受影響；包裝場損失量仍是缺口","Intervention mechanism":"介入機制","Living-cell VOC headspace screen → risk-tier output → human decision → confirmatory assay when escalated":"活細胞 VOC 頂空篩檢 → 風險分級輸出 → 人員決策 → 升級處理時進行確認性試驗","Positive pathway":"正面路徑","Earlier triage could reduce unnecessary full-lot discard and protect income":"較早分流可能減少不必要的整批丟棄，並保護所得，前提是","accuracy, trust, and access hold":"準確率、信任與取得機會皆成立","Negative pathway":"負面路徑","False negatives → overtrust harm; false positives → excess discard; biology / plastics / e-waste / cold-chain burden; smallholder fear of being flagged":"偽陰性 → 過度信任傷害；偽陽性 → 額外丟棄；生物／塑膠／電子廢棄物／冷鏈負擔；小農害怕被標記","Evidence type":"證據類型","for loss reduction ·":"：減少損失 ·","for mechanism ·":"：機制 ·","for buyer shift ·":"：買方轉移 ·","for field performance & LCA":"：現場效能與生命週期評估","Current measurement":"目前量測","No field loss reduction measured. The early n = 28 summary informs education; the later reported total of 107 does not yet support new item-level findings. Hardware validation pending.":"尚未量測現場損失減少。早期 n = 28 摘要引導教育；後期回報總數 107 尚不能支持新的逐題發現。硬體驗證待完成。","Uncertainty":"不確定性","VOC detectability in field air; payer economics; cartridge lifetime; net footprint vs destructive assays; packing-house workflow fit":"現場空氣中的 VOC 可偵測性；付費者經濟條件；匣體壽命；相較破壞性試驗的淨足跡；與包裝場工作流程的相容性","Exporter / packing-house interviews; hardware power & optical ladder; cartridge reuse protocol; minimal LCA + wet-lab waste log":"出口商／包裝場訪談；硬體功耗與光學驗證階梯；匣體重用流程；最小生命週期評估與濕實驗廢棄物記錄","Blank reusable version":"空白可重用版本","Copy into your notebook or wiki. No server download — clipboard only.":"複製到你的筆記本或 網站。僅使用剪貼簿，不從伺服器下載。","Copy template":"複製範本","[ Measured | Stakeholder-backed | Estimated | Designed | Hypothesis | Open gap ]":"[ 已量測 | 利害關係人支持 | 估計 | 已設計 | 假說 | 待補缺口 ]","Companion method notes (optional)":"補充方法筆記（選用）","Scope split:":"範圍區分：","keep track science visually distinct from commercial beachhead claims.":"在視覺上區分各路線科學與商業灘頭堡主張。","Change cards:":"改變卡片：","Thought → Heard → Changed → Still open; photos alone are not evidence.":"原本想法 → 聽到的意見 → 做出的改變 → 仍未解決；照片本身不是證據。","Architecture currency:":"架構現況：","sync Hardware before writing efficiency claims; do not resurrect retired subsystems.":"撰寫效率主張之前，先同步硬體現況；不要重新加入已淘汰子系統。","Self-footprint first:":"先看自身足跡：","inventory your own consumables before claiming you reduce others’ waste.":"在宣稱減少他人廢棄物之前，先盤點自己的耗材。","12 · Next":"12 · 下一步","Each open question needs a baseline, an explicit target and a record that can be checked. The plan below follows the Sustainability source while retaining the later hardware and survey corrections. Targets are planned work, not achieved results.":"每個未解問題，都需要基準、明確目標與可檢查記錄。下方計畫依循永續來源內容，同時保留後續硬體與問卷修正。目標代表規劃工作，不是已達成成果。","Swipe across the table to compare evidence and next steps.":"橫向滑動表格，比較證據與下一步。","Measurement plan: current evidence, next target and outcome to record.":"量測計畫：目前證據、下一個目標與應記錄結果。","Current evidence":"目前證據","Target / next step":"目標／下一步","Detection lead time · Track A":"偵測提前時間 · 路線 A","No matched VOC / visual-onset dataset.":"尚無配對的 VOC／目視症狀出現資料集。","Measure days gained relative to visible symptoms. Set an improvement target after live-cell validation.":"量測相對於可見症狀多獲得幾天。在活細胞驗證後再設定改善目標。","Reader power":"讀取器功耗","Operating power unmeasured. Below 1 W is a draft design aspiration.":"操作功耗尚未量測。低於 1 W 是草稿中的設計願景。","Measure power at each validation stage; state what is powered and include the biological workflow separately.":"在每個驗證階段量測功耗；說明哪些設備有供電，並另行納入生物流程。","Cartridge replacement interval":"感測匣更換間隔","No lifetime test. An industry anecdote about near-daily replacement is not a general comparator baseline.":"尚無壽命測試。產業中幾乎每天更換的個別敘述，不能作為通用比較基準。","Measure days and valid readings per cartridge under stated storage and use conditions.":"在明確儲存與使用條件下，量測每個匣體的天數與有效讀取次數。","Wet-lab footprint":"濕實驗足跡","Plastic mass, consumable quantities and reagent hazard classes have not been tallied.":"塑膠質量、耗材用量與試劑危害類別尚未統計。","Complete a waste and hazard audit before wiki freeze; record mass in kg and segregation / inactivation practices.":"在 網站 定稿前完成廢棄物與危害稽核；以 kg 記錄質量，並記錄分類／去活化實務。","Screening life-cycle assessment":"初步生命週期評估","No completed comparison or net-benefit result.":"尚無完成的比較或淨效益結果。","Complete one screening LCA against a defined existing workflow using the":"使用下列內容，與明確的既有流程完成一次初步生命週期評估：","inventory and functional unit":"盤查清單與功能單位","Survey and risk-tier communication · Track B":"問卷與風險分級溝通 · 路線 B","Early n = 28 aggregate; later n = 107 team reported, with no updated item-level analysis.":"早期 n = 28 彙整；後期 n = 107 為團隊回報，無更新的逐題分析。","Reconcile response counts and denominators, then test interpretation and escalation decisions with users.":"核對回覆人數與分母，再與使用者測試解讀及升級處理決策。","Exporter / packing-house input":"出口商／包裝場意見","No direct buyer interview on record.":"無直接買方訪談記錄。","At least one interview with batch-level loss, workflow, payer and benefit information.":"至少一場包含批次損失、工作流程、付費者與受益資訊的訪談。","Industry collaboration":"產業合作","Completed knowledge-sharing interviews; a separate company visit is prepared. No formal contract claimed.":"已完成知識共享訪談；另一次公司參訪已準備。不宣稱有正式合約。","At least one formal partnership conversation with scope, responsibilities and next steps recorded.":"至少一場正式夥伴關係對話，並記錄範圍、責任與下一步。","Impact and future plan":"影響與未來計畫","Social":"社會","Test shared institutional access and plain-language risk tiers with the farmers, cooperatives and operators who would use them.":"與未來使用的農民、合作社及操作人員，測試機構共用取得方式與白話風險分級。","Economic":"經濟","Build a buyer-specific cost model before claiming savings, and check whether value flows from institutions to smallholders.":"在宣稱節省成本前，先建立特定買方成本模型，並檢查價值是否從機構流向小農。","Environmental":"環境","Measure retained food, recurring biological inputs and end-of-life burdens together. Food-loss prevention is a hypothesis until the workflow comparison supports it.":"共同量測保留食品、持續生物投入與生命終期負擔。在流程比較支持之前，預防食品損失仍是假說。","Our contribution today is a research direction shaped by external input, with its trade-offs made explicit. The":"我們目前的貢獻，是受到外部意見塑造、並明確呈現取捨的研究方向。","reusable evidence canvas":"可重用證據畫布","lets future teams extend the measurements without treating today’s plans as completed validation.":"讓未來團隊延伸量測，而不把今天的計畫當成已完成驗證。","Source record and update notes":"來源記錄與更新筆記","This page was reconciled with the team’s public Sustainability Notion page on 12 October 2026. Its four supplied SDG images and two-track framing are retained. Track A is the export supply chain; Track B is stored food.":"本頁於 2026 年 10 月 12 日，與團隊公開的 Sustainability Notion 頁面核對整合。保留其提供的四張 SDG 圖片與雙路線架構。路線 A 是出口供應鏈，路線 B 是儲存食品。","The source’s Raspberry Pi + ESP32 line is superseded by the current ESP32-standalone Hardware design.":"來源中的 Raspberry Pi＋ESP32 架構，已由目前硬體的 ESP32 獨立式設計取代。","The early n = 28 survey and later reported total of 107 remain separate. The source’s 100% discard statement has no verified item-level basis here.":"早期 n = 28 問卷與後期回報總數 107 維持分開。來源中的 100% 丟棄說法，在此沒有已核實的逐題依據。","The below-1 W value is a design aspiration, and NT$3.51 billion is a team sizing estimate. Neither is a measured sustainability benefit.":"低於 1 W 是設計願景，新臺幣 35.1 億元是團隊規模估計。兩者都不是實測永續效益。","Draft placeholders for lead time, cartridge lifetime and laboratory waste remain open measurements; no missing figures have been filled with estimates.":"草稿中偵測提前時間、匣體壽命與實驗室廢棄物的占位項，仍是待完成量測；沒有以估計值填補缺失數字。","End of Human Practices arc":"人文實踐故事線結束","e.g. SDG, trade-off, LCA, beachhead":"例如：SDG、取捨、生命週期評估、灘頭堡市場","Track A export supply chain and Track B stored food":"路線 A 出口供應鏈與路線 B 儲存食品","Sustainability reading path":"永續閱讀路徑","Pathway node detail":"路徑節點詳情","Relationship maturity labels":"關係成熟度標籤","SDG 2 · Zero Hunger":"SDG 2 · 消除飢餓","SDG 9 · Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure":"SDG 9 · 產業、創新與基礎設施","SDG 12 · Responsible Consumption and Production":"SDG 12 · 責任消費與生產","SDG 17 · Partnerships for the Goals":"SDG 17 · 夥伴關係","Relationship types":"關係類型","SDG interaction matrix (visual overview; use cards below for full text)":"SDG 互動矩陣（視覺概覽；完整文字請見下方卡片）","SDG 2 Zero Hunger":"SDG 2 消除飢餓","SDG 3 Good Health":"SDG 3 健康","SDG 9 Industry Innovation":"SDG 9 產業創新","SDG 10 Reduced Inequalities":"SDG 10 減少不平等","SDG 12 Responsible Consumption":"SDG 12 責任消費","SDG 17 Partnerships":"SDG 17 夥伴關係","SDG relationships as cards":"以卡片呈現的 SDG 關係","SDG relationship detail":"SDG 關係詳情","Impact model: definitions, units and sensitivity":"影響模型：定義、單位與敏感度","Benefit and exclusion matrix":"效益與排除矩陣","Sustainability measurement plan":"永續量測計畫","Sustainable Development Impact · AeroSense · NTHU iGEM 2026":"永續發展影響 · AeroSense · NTHU iGEM 2026","Laboratory development, an archived 28-response survey and a later team-reported survey of 300 respondents.":"實驗室開發、封存的 28 份回覆問卷，以及團隊後續回報的 300 人問卷。","Early survey informed teaching; 300 respondents in the later summary":"早期問卷影響教學設計；後續摘要回報 300 人","The early 28-response survey informed teaching design. The later 300-respondent summary adds self-reported knowledge and storage habits; neither measures learning gains.":"早期 28 份問卷影響教學設計。後續 300 人摘要補充自陳知識與儲存習慣；兩者都不是學習增益的量測。","Early 28-response survey; later 300-respondent summary":"早期 28 份回覆問卷；後續 300 人摘要","Food storage and mold-risk perception · archived n = 28; later team-reported n = 300":"食品儲存與黴菌風險認知 · 封存 n = 28；團隊後續回報 n = 300","The later Education summary reports 78% understanding the mold-removal limitation, 64% the heating limitation and 58% the look-and-smell limitation. These are self-reported aggregates from 300 respondents; raw responses and item-level denominators are not supplied.":"後續 Education 摘要回報：78% 理解去除黴菌的限制、64% 理解加熱的限制、58% 理解外觀與氣味判斷的限制。這些是 300 位受訪者的自陳彙整資料；來源未提供原始回覆與逐題有效人數。","· archived n = 28 and later n = 300 are distinct records. No paired learning effect or population prevalence is inferred.":"· 封存 n = 28 與後續 n = 300 是不同紀錄；不據此推論配對學習效果或整體人口比例。","The archived 28-response survey informed initial teaching. Education also reports the later n = 300 aggregate, separately from the early exact counts.":"封存的 28 份回覆問卷影響初期教學。Education 另列後續 n = 300 彙整資料，與早期精確計數分開呈現。","Survey records inform teaching and communication; they do not quantify avoided food loss, carbon savings or learning gains.":"問卷紀錄用於教學與溝通設計；它們不量化減少的食品損失、碳排節省或學習增益。","SDG 4 · reusable education":"SDG 4 · 可重用教育","document the outcome of the proposed company discussion and develop one peer-team exchange into a joint activity.":"記錄規劃中的公司討論結果，並將一項跨隊交流發展為共同活動。","Our source identifies SDGs 2, 9, 12 and 17 as primary goals. SDGs 3, 4 and 10 connect screening boundaries, reusable education and equitable access. The SDGs organize our questions; they do not establish impact.":"來源將 SDG 2、9、12、17 列為主要目標；SDG 3、4、10 則連結篩檢範圍、可重用教育與公平近用。SDGs 用來整理問題，並不是影響成效的證明。","SDG 4 — Quality Education":"SDG 4 — 優質教育","SDG 4 — Quality Education: make food-risk reasoning and biological sensing understandable and reusable.":"SDG 4 優質教育：讓食品風險推理與生物感測知識易於理解、便於重用。","A free five-module Learning Lab, browser activities and facilitator guidance connect everyday decisions to the sensing system.":"免費的五模組 Learning Lab、瀏覽器活動與帶領者指南，將日常決策連結至感測系統。","Evidence":"證據","The team reports a rural elementary-school science camp on 12 October and an NTHU student workshop on 14 October 2026, alongside the 8 October peer-team exchange.":"團隊回報於 2026 年 10 月 12 日舉辦偏鄉小學科學營、10 月 14 日舉辦清大學生工作坊，並於 10 月 8 日參與跨隊交流。","Activity records and survey responses do not demonstrate a learning gain. Completed paired learning-outcome data are not supplied.":"活動紀錄與問卷回覆無法證明學習增益；來源尚未提供完整的配對學習成效資料。","Record participation, paired assessment counts, missing responses and how participant feedback changes the next teaching session.":"記錄參與情形、配對評量人數、缺失回覆，以及參與者回饋如何改變下一次教學。","Education · activities, survey and reuse":"Education · 活動、問卷與重用","Peer teams and learners":"其他團隊與學習者","8 October 2026 · TAU-Israel mini jamboree; 12 October · rural elementary-school science camp; 14 October · NTHU student workshop.":"2026 年 10 月 8 日 · TAU-Israel mini jamboree；10 月 12 日 · 偏鄉小學科學營；10 月 14 日 · 清大學生工作坊。","These are team-reported exchanges and teaching activities. They are not joint research projects or commercial partnerships. The source has not yet specified which mini-jamboree feedback changed the model or curriculum.":"這些是團隊回報的交流與教學活動，並非共同研究計畫或商業合作。來源尚未具體說明 mini jamboree 的哪些回饋改變了模型或課程。","Read the activity records and evaluation limits":"閱讀活動紀錄與評估限制","Patent advice and open science":"專利建議與開放科學","The Notion account adds a completed conversation with a patent attorney. The team describes preparing a university filing and sequencing disclosure around that process; it does not report a filed or granted patent.":"Notion 紀錄新增了與專利律師的已完成討論。團隊描述正準備透過學校提出申請，並安排資訊揭露順序；來源並未回報已提出申請或取得專利。","The sustainability question is who can access the resulting technology. Restrictive licensing or pricing could exclude associations and smallholders. Reusable education materials can remain openly available while the team records what technical material is released and when.":"永續性的問題是誰能取得這項技術。限制性授權或定價可能排除協會與小農。團隊可持續開放可重用教材，同時記錄哪些技術資料已發布及其時間。","Taoyuan District Agricultural Improvement Station · Plant Protection Lab; Taiwan Banana Research Institute also named in the updated source":"桃園區農業改良場 · 植物保護研究室；更新來源另列台灣香蕉研究所","Upstream agricultural institutions helped frame disease and post-harvest handling. The updated source names the Taiwan Banana Research Institute but leaves its specific design influence undocumented. Exporter-side loss volumes still need direct validation.":"上游農業機構協助釐清病害與採後處理問題。更新來源列出台灣香蕉研究所，但尚未記錄其對設計的具體影響；出口端損失量仍需直接驗證。","The updated source counts four industry conversations, including a patent attorney, as knowledge-sharing. Formal e-nose company discussions and exploratory contact with the S.Y.Dao Cancer Prevention Foundation remain prospective, with no commitment reported.":"更新來源將包含專利律師在內的四次業界對話列為知識交流。與電子鼻公司的正式討論，以及與 S.Y.Dao Cancer Prevention Foundation 的探索性聯繫，仍屬潛在合作；來源未回報任何承諾。","Document the proposed industry discussion, turn one peer exchange into a joint activity, and report the scope and responsibilities of any resulting collaboration.":"記錄規劃中的業界討論、將一項跨隊交流發展為共同活動，並說明任何後續合作的範圍與責任。","Survey interpretation":"問卷解讀","The later Education source reports n = 300 and rounded percentages. The earlier n = 28 exact counts remain archived. Sample overlap, item denominators and raw responses are not supplied; do not combine the two records or infer national prevalence.":"後續 Education 來源回報 n = 300 與四捨五入百分比。早期 n = 28 的精確計數仍保留。來源未提供樣本重疊、逐題有效人數與原始回覆；不得合併兩筆紀錄或推論全國比例。","Open supporting record":"開啟支持紀錄","Sector exposure estimate":"產業風險金額估計","The Notion source frames approximately NT$3.51 billion per year as 33.6% of NT$10.445 billion in sector output. This is a team sector-risk estimate, not observed batch loss, the addressable market, or an AeroSense saving.":"Notion 來源將每年約新台幣 35.1 億元描述為產業產值 104.45 億元的 33.6%。這是團隊的產業風險估計，並非實測批次損失、可服務市場或 AeroSense 節省額。","Estimate, not savings":"估計值，並非節省額","Detection lead time":"偵測提前時間","Earlier warning than visible symptoms is an application hypothesis. Compare matched lots with a defined symptom threshold and confirmation method before setting a lead-time target.":"比可見症狀更早發出警示是應用假設；須以明確症狀門檻及確認方法比較配對批次，再設定提前時間目標。","Not measured":"尚未量測","Cartridge lifetime":"匣體壽命","Repeated use and lower replacement frequency are design intentions. Define usable sensitivity, drift and contamination limits, then measure lifetime across independent cartridges.":"重複使用與降低更換頻率是設計意圖；須定義可接受靈敏度、漂移與污染界限，再以獨立匣體量測壽命。","Laboratory waste inventory":"實驗室廢棄物盤點","The source calls for reagent hazard classes and plastic waste mass, but supplies no audit figures. Record quantities, segregation and inactivation routes before claiming a reduction.":"來源要求記錄試劑危害分類與塑膠廢棄物重量，但未提供盤點數據；應先記錄數量、分類及去活化處理方式，再主張減量。","Unquantified":"尚未量化","Net environmental benefit":"淨環境效益","No completed comparative life-cycle assessment is available. The per-tonne framework includes the reader, cell culture, cartridge, energy, confirmation and disposal alongside any food retained.":"目前無完整比較生命週期評估。每噸食品的比較架構，除保留食品外，也納入讀取器、細胞培養、匣體、能源、確認檢測與處置。","No completed LCA":"尚無完整生命週期評估","Reader power and calibration":"讀取器功耗與校正","Current Hardware documents a physical assembled reader. Assembly photographs and simulations do not measure operating power, channel crosstalk or field robustness.":"目前 Hardware 記錄實體組裝讀取器；組裝照片與模擬不等於操作功耗、通道串擾或現場穩健性的量測。","Measurement pending":"待量測","Complete biological readout":"完整生物讀取流程","The P2 experiment used a laboratory plate reader and one well per condition. No paired measurements connect that experiment to the assembled AeroSense reader; it does not establish end-to-end performance.":"P2 實驗使用實驗室盤式讀取器，每個條件僅有一孔。目前沒有配對量測連結該實驗與組裝完成的 AeroSense 讀取器，因此不構成端到端效能證據。","End-to-end validation pending":"待端到端驗證","Screening boundary":"篩檢主張範圍","A VOC signal is not a food-safety or mycotoxin verdict. Low-risk output must not be presented as proof that a portion is safe; concerning results require an appropriate confirmatory workflow.":"VOC 訊號不是食品安全或真菌毒素判定。低風險輸出不得當作食品安全的證明；可疑結果須進入適當的確認檢測流程。","Confirmation required":"須確認檢測","Access and disclosure":"近用與資訊揭露","Patent advice informs the team’s proposed disclosure sequence. Filing, licensing terms and equitable access are not established outcomes. Track both reusable releases and who can afford the technology.":"專利建議影響團隊規劃的揭露順序；申請、授權條件與公平近用尚非已完成成果。應同時追蹤可重用成果發布及誰能負擔技術。","Trade-off documented":"已記錄取捨","Engagement maturity":"交流成熟程度","Field interviews, academic research, industry conversations, mentorship and learner exchanges are distinct forms of engagement. The source reports no commercial commitment; exporter and packing-house interviews remain missing.":"實地訪談、學術研究、業界討論、導師指導及學習者交流是不同形式的接觸。來源未回報商業承諾；出口商與包裝場訪談仍未完成。","No commercial partnership claimed":"不主張商業合作已成立","documents the current PCB, assembled enclosure and validation procedure. These establish build progress, not power or field performance.":"記錄目前的 PCB、已組裝外殼及驗證程序；這些證明製作進度，並不代表功耗或現場效能。","Source reconciliation · 18 October 2026":"來源比對 · 2026 年 10 月 18 日","The Sustainability and Education Notion pages were read on 18 October 2026. Their updated survey and engagement records are incorporated here. The original Notion pages are unchanged.":"本頁於 2026 年 10 月 18 日讀取 Sustainability 與 Education Notion 頁面，納入更新問卷與交流紀錄；原始 Notion 頁面未經修改。","The Sustainability draft still describes fabrication as pending. The current Hardware page contains PCB and assembled-reader photographs, so this wiki uses that build record while keeping power, optical calibration and end-to-end validation open.":"Sustainability 草稿仍寫著待製作；目前 Hardware 頁面已含 PCB 與組裝讀取器照片，因此網站依製作紀錄更新進度，仍將功耗、光學校正與端到端驗證列為待完成。","The later Education summary reports 300 respondents. It does not establish how those respondents relate to the archived 28-response survey. Percentages remain reported aggregates, not reconstructed exact counts or before/after learning results.":"後續 Education 摘要回報 300 位受訪者，但未說明其與封存 28 份問卷的關係。百分比保留為來源彙整值，不重建精確計數，也不視為學習前後測結果。","Public Notion page, retrieved 18 October 2026.":"公開 Notion 頁面，於 2026 年 10 月 18 日讀取。","Source review: 18 October 2026. This page incorporates the updated survey and engagement records from the Sustainability and Education team accounts.":"來源檢視日期：2026 年 10 月 18 日。本頁納入團隊 Sustainability 與 Education 紀錄更新的問卷及交流內容。","Source and relevance":"來源與關聯","Claim":"主張","The ledger separates measurements, stakeholder input, estimates, designs and open hypotheses. Each entry states the evidence available and the limit on its interpretation.":"此清單區分量測、利害關係人回饋、估算、設計與待驗證假設；各項列明現有證據及解讀限制。","The ledger links documented decisions and design outputs to their sources.":"此表將已記錄的決策與設計產出連結至來源。","Documented inputs and design decisions, with links to the full record.":"已記錄的意見與設計決策，並連結完整記錄。","Survey-guided teaching":"問卷引導教學","Survey":"問卷","Curriculum decision":"課程決策","Decisions documented":"決策已記錄","Reader architecture":"讀取器架構","Decision design":"決策設計","Modular architecture":"模組化架構","Open evidence and limits":"展開證據與限制","Fold pathway":"收合路徑","The archived 28-response survey informed the initial education redesign. The later summary identifies continuing questions for teaching and risk-tier communication; it is not evidence that the redesign caused a learning gain.":"封存的 28 份回覆問卷影響初期教育改版。後續摘要指出教學與風險分級溝通仍需處理的問題，但不證明改版帶來了學習增益。","What do we mean by sustainability?":"我們所說的永續性是什麼？","Sustainability is not a property a product either has or lacks. It describes how ecological, economic, and social systems interact over time. Because these systems are interconnected, sustainability problems are often called \"wicked problems\": no single correct answer, and no single discipline can solve them [3]. This makes sustainability a matter of systems thinking — a change in one part of a system can have unexpected effects elsewhere — and of resilience, the capacity to adapt while retaining core function, which matters as much as efficiency.":"永續性不是一項產品非有即無的特性。它描述生態、經濟和社會系統如何隨時間互相影響。由於這些系統彼此相連，永續性問題常被稱為「棘手問題」：沒有單一正確答案，也沒有任何單一學科能夠解決它們 [3]。因此，永續性涉及系統思考——系統某一部分的改變，可能在其他地方產生意料之外的影響——也涉及韌性，也就是在保留核心功能的同時適應變化的能力；這與效率同樣重要。","The Brundtland definition (1987) — meeting present needs without compromising the ability of future generations to meet theirs [1] — is simple and communicable, but criticized as anthropocentric. The \"three pillars\" model (environmental, social, economic) complements it by stressing their interdependence. The UN SDGs [2] turn these ideas into 17 goals for 2030; they are ambitious and criticized for breadth, but they are the common language iGEM teams use, so we adopt them while staying aware of their limits.":"布倫特蘭的定義（1987 年）——滿足當代需求，同時不損及後代滿足自身需求的能力 [1]——簡單且易於傳達，但也被批評為以人類為中心。「三大支柱」模型（環境、社會、經濟）強調三者相互依存，補充了這項定義。聯合國永續發展目標（SDGs）[2] 將這些想法轉化為 2030 年前的 17 項目標；它們雄心勃勃，也因涵蓋範圍廣泛而受到批評，但它們是 iGEM 團隊使用的共同語言，因此我們採用這套目標，同時留意其侷限。","AeroSense and sustainable development":"AeroSense 與永續發展","AeroSense is an AI-driven, biologically inspired VOC (volatile organic compound) sensing platform: a living olfactory-receptor layer, custom lock-in optoelectronic hardware, and a neuromorphic classifier modeled on the fly brain, packaged as a portable, cartridge-based electronic nose. We work on two layers and keep them separate throughout this page:":"AeroSense 是一個由 AI 驅動、受生物啟發的 VOC（揮發性有機化合物）感測平台：由活體嗅覺受體層、客製化鎖相光電硬體，以及以果蠅大腦為模型的神經形態分類器組成，整合為使用匣式感測元件的可攜式電子鼻。我們在兩個層次上開展工作，並在整個頁面中將它們分開：","Application theme — stored food (Food & Nutrition track). Mold- and pathogen-VOC screening in stored tea, coffee, and other dried foods. Our public survey and most of our education work belong here.":"應用主題——儲存食品（Food & Nutrition 賽道）。針對儲存的茶葉、咖啡及其他乾燥食品，進行黴菌與病原體 VOC 篩檢。我們的公眾問卷與大部分教育工作都屬於這個層次。","Commercial beachhead — fruit export supply chain. Early detection of fungal disease and ripeness in Taiwan's banana and mango exports, with tea processing as the second-stage expansion. Its buyers are institutions (exporters, packing houses, associations) rather than individual consumers, which is why we entered here first.":"商業切入市場——水果出口供應鏈。及早偵測臺灣出口香蕉與芒果的真菌病害和成熟度，並將茶葉加工列為第二階段的擴展方向。買方是機構（出口商、包裝場、協會），而非個別消費者，這也是我們首先切入此處的原因。","We asked not only whether the technology could work, but whether it should, for whom, and at what cost to which other goal. Our Human Practices engagement shaped the answers: the Taoyuan District Agricultural Improvement Station's Plant Protection Lab, the Taiwan Banana Research Institute, farmers' associations and facility farms, an electronic-nose company's Chief Science Officer, Chia-Nien Biotechnology, an analytical-instrumentation (GC-MS/LC-MS) professional, a patent attorney, our academic advisors, and the pupils, students, and peer teams we taught and learned from.":"我們不只詢問這項技術是否可行，也詢問它是否應該被採用、為誰服務，以及會讓其他哪項目標付出什麼代價。我們的 Human Practices 交流形塑了答案：參與者包括桃園區農業改良場植物保護研究室、財團法人台灣香蕉研究所、農會與設施農場、某電子鼻公司的首席科學官、Chia-Nien Biotechnology、一位分析儀器（GC-MS／LC-MS）專業人士、一位專利律師、我們的學術指導老師，以及我們教導並向其學習的小學生、大學生與其他團隊。","We anchor this page on four goals our work has actually touched — SDG 2, 9, 12, and 17 — with SDG 3, 4, and 10 as supporting connections. We are at a preliminary stage: no full life-cycle assessment, cost analysis, or market study yet, and hardware validation is still in progress. This page is therefore critical reflection, not a promise.":"本頁以我們的工作實際觸及的四項目標——SDG 2、9、12 和 17——為核心，並以 SDG 3、4 和 10 作為補充連結。我們仍處於初步階段：尚未完成完整的生命週期評估、成本分析或市場研究，硬體驗證也仍在進行。因此，本頁是批判性的反思，而非承諾。","Our SDGs at a glance":"我們的 SDGs 概覽","SDG / Target":"SDG／細項目標","What AeroSense does":"AeroSense 的工作","Evidence so far":"目前的證據","Metric and next step":"指標與下一步","2.4 Resilient agriculture":"2.4 韌性農業","Flags disease/ripeness VOC signals before symptoms are visible, so batches can be isolated or rerouted":"在症狀可見之前標示病害／成熟度 VOC 訊號，讓批次能夠被隔離或改變去向","Field interviews; estimated NT$3.51B/yr risk (33.6% of NT$10.445B sector output)":"田野訪談；估計每年風險為新臺幣 35.1 億元（產業產值新臺幣 104.45 億元的 33.6%）","Detection lead time vs. visual symptoms; interview an exporter or packing house":"相對於可見症狀的偵測提前時間；訪談出口商或包裝場","2.3 Small-scale producer income":"2.3 小規模生產者收入","Targets associations and cooperatives, not individual farmers":"以協會與合作社為對象，而非個別農民","Instrumentation interview: low farmer willingness to pay":"儀器業訪談：農民付費意願低","Cost model showing who pays and who benefits":"呈現由誰付費、由誰受益的成本模型","9.5 Research and technological capability":"9.5 研究與技術能力","Living receptor sensing element plus fly-mushroom-body classifier":"活體受體感測元件加上果蠅蘑菇體分類器","E-nose CSO interview; Sci. Adv. 2025 [10]":"電子鼻首席科學官訪談；Sci. Adv. 2025 [10]","Live-cell end-to-end validation":"活細胞端到端驗證","9.b Domestic technology development":"9.b 本土技術發展","In-house readout: four modulated LEDs, one shared photodiode, and an ESP32 that runs the lock-in":"自行開發讀取系統：四個調變 LED、一個共用光電二極體，以及執行鎖相的 ESP32","Housing and circuit board designed (CAD and layout); fabrication and assembly pending; power not yet measured":"外殼與電路板已設計（CAD 與佈線）；製作與組裝待完成；尚未量測功耗","Fabricate and assemble; measure noise rejection, crosstalk, and power at each validation stage":"製作與組裝；在每個驗證階段量測雜訊抑制、串擾與功耗","12.3 Food loss":"12.3 食物損失","Risk-tier output instead of binary discard":"輸出風險分級，而非二元的丟棄決定","Public survey (stored-food theme, directional): only 58% understood that a normal look and smell does not mean no risk":"公眾問卷（儲存食品主題，提供方向）：只有 58% 理解外觀與氣味正常並不代表沒有風險","Add shop and warehouse perspectives; test tier output with users":"加入商店與倉庫的觀點；與使用者測試分級輸出","12.5 Waste prevention":"12.5 廢棄物預防","Non-destructive, reusable cartridge":"非破壞性、可重複使用的感測匣","Design intent only":"僅為設計意圖","Cartridge lifetime test; screening LCA":"感測匣壽命測試；初步生命週期評估","12.4 Chemicals and waste":"12.4 化學品與廢棄物","Wet-lab footprint self-audit":"濕實驗室環境足跡自我稽核","Not yet started":"尚未開始","Audit before wiki freeze":"在 wiki 凍結前完成稽核","17.16 / 17.17 Partnerships":"17.16／17.17 夥伴關係","Field, academic, industry, and peer-team knowledge-sharing":"田野、學術、產業與其他團隊的知識分享","Four completed industry conversations (including a patent attorney); published advisor paper; one cross-team exchange":"已完成四次產業對話（含一位專利律師）；指導老師已發表論文；一次跨團隊交流","One formal industry partnership conversation; one joint activity with another team":"一次正式產業合作對話；與另一團隊舉辦一次聯合活動","Commercial beachhead. Catching disease-affected produce earlier and timing ripeness decisions reduces food loss along the supply chain.":"商業切入市場。更早發現受到病害影響的農產品，並掌握成熟度決策的時機，可減少供應鏈中的食物損失。","Target 2.4 — Resilient agricultural practices. Informed by our field interviews [6], we estimate fungal-disease-related risk in Taiwan's banana and mango export sector at roughly NT$3.51 billion/year (about 33.6% of NT$10.445 billion annual output value). Today's detection is either visual sampling — by which point infection has often spread — or slow, destructive lab assays that cannot cover a whole shipment. Flagging a VOC signal before symptoms appear lets exporters, packing houses, and cooperatives isolate, reroute, or re-time a batch instead of losing it. Globally, roughly 14% of food is lost between harvest and retail [4], so the supply-chain link we target is a known weak point, not a niche one.":"目標 2.4——具韌性的農業實踐。根據田野訪談 [6]，我們估計臺灣香蕉與芒果出口產業中與真菌病害相關的風險約為每年新臺幣 35.1 億元（約占新臺幣 104.45 億元年產值的 33.6%）。目前的偵測方式不是目視抽樣——到了那時，感染往往已經擴散——就是緩慢且具破壞性的實驗室檢測，無法涵蓋整批出貨。在症狀出現之前標示 VOC 訊號，讓出口商、包裝場與合作社能夠隔離批次、改變去向或調整時程，而非失去整批產品。全球約有 14% 的食物在收穫至零售之間損失 [4]，因此我們鎖定的供應鏈環節是已知的薄弱點，而非小眾問題。","[Insert quantified batch-level loss data once an exporter or packing house has been interviewed. So far we have interviewed only agricultural institutions upstream of them.]Next step: interview at least one exporter or packing house, and measure detection lead time against visual symptom onset in validation.":"[待訪談出口商或包裝場後，插入量化的批次損失數據。目前我們只訪談了其上游的農業機構。]下一步：訪談至少一位出口商或一處包裝場，並在驗證時量測相對於可見症狀出現的偵測提前時間。","Target 2.3 — Productivity and incomes of small-scale producers. This is the tension we have to be honest about. The instrumentation professional we interviewed [9] expected low willingness to pay among individual farmers, and a device sold directly to smallholders would add cost without adding income. Selling to associations and cooperatives lets a smallholder's income protection come from a shared, institution-level tool they do not have to buy or fear — but this is a design intention, not a validated outcome. Next step: a cost model that shows who pays, who benefits, and whether the benefit reaches smallholders.":"目標 2.3——小規模生產者的生產力與收入。這是我們必須誠實面對的矛盾。我們訪談的儀器業專業人士 [9] 預期個別農民的付費意願偏低，而直接售予小農的裝置會增加成本，卻不會增加收入。售予協會與合作社，能讓小農的收入保障來自一項共用的機構層級工具，而他們不必自行購買或感到畏懼——但這是設計意圖，並非已驗證的成果。 下一步：建立成本模型，呈現由誰付費、由誰受益，以及效益是否能到達小農。","SDG 9 — Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure":"SDG 9——產業、創新與基礎建設","AeroSense integrates biological sensing, custom optoelectronics, and neuromorphic AI into a field-deployable platform built on the team's own peer-reviewed research.":"AeroSense 以團隊自身經同儕審查的研究為基礎，將生物感測、客製化光電技術與神經形態 AI，整合為可於現場部署的平台。","Target 9.5 — Research and technological capability. The e-nose CSO told us the industry bottleneck is the sensing element — selectivity, sensitivity, lifetime, reproducibility [7]. AeroSense responds with a living, self-renewing receptor (Drosophila OR/Orco with the GCaMP6 reporter in a standard mammalian cell line), structurally different from a static chemical film. Our classifier is modeled on the fly mushroom body's PN–KC–MBON circuit and has a direct published lineage through our advisors' Science Advances paper [10], which is open access (CC BY 4.0), with code on Dryad and data on Zenodo.":"目標 9.5——研究與技術能力。電子鼻公司的首席科學官告訴我們，產業瓶頸在於感測元件——選擇性、靈敏度、壽命與再現性 [7]。AeroSense 以活體、能自我更新的受體回應此問題（在標準哺乳類細胞株中表現果蠅 OR／Orco 與 GCaMP6 報導蛋白），其結構不同於靜態化學薄膜。我們的分類器以果蠅蘑菇體的 PN–KC–MBON 迴路為模型，並直接承襲指導老師已發表於 Science Advances 的論文 [10]；該論文採開放取用（CC BY 4.0），程式碼存於 Dryad，資料存於 Zenodo。","Target 9.b — Domestic technology development. Our first readout used a blue LED and a camera (CMOS, 30 frames per second). It worked on the bench, but outside the lab ambient light and sensor noise swamped a faint cell signal, which is what the e-nose industry had warned us about. We replaced it with an in-house design: four LEDs, each modulated at its own frequency, excite four wells that share one photodiode, and an ESP32 runs digital lock-in detection to read each channel while rejecting room light and slow drift. We state its limits as plainly. Excitation light that leaks onto the detector at the same frequency as the signal survives lock-in, and because the wells share one detector and a gas space, physical mixing between wells still needs calibration, so emission filtering, blank wells, and per-well calibration are still required. The housing and circuit board exist only as CAD and layout, with fabrication and full assembly pending, so we have not yet measured the platform's power draw or noise performance, and we do not yet know its net footprint against the biological layer (culture media, consumables, cold chain). Validation is planned in five stages — component bench tests, electronics-only lock-in, fluorescent-dye calibration, environmental-noise robustness, live-cell end-to-end — and is not complete. Next step: fabricate and assemble the board, then report measured noise rejection, crosstalk, and power at each stage as it completes.":"目標 9.b——本土技術發展。我們最初的讀取系統使用藍色 LED 與相機（CMOS，每秒 30 影格）。它在實驗桌上能夠運作，但在實驗室外，環境光與感測器雜訊淹沒了微弱的細胞訊號，這正是電子鼻產業曾提醒我們的問題。我們以自行開發的設計取代它：四個 LED 各以不同頻率調變，激發四個共用一顆光電二極體的孔洞，再由 ESP32 執行數位鎖相偵測，讀取各通道，同時排除室內光線與緩慢漂移。我們也同樣清楚陳述其限制。以相同訊號頻率漏到偵測器上的激發光會通過鎖相偵測，而且由於各孔共用同一個偵測器與氣體空間，孔間的物理混合仍需校正，因此仍需要放射光濾光、空白孔與逐孔校正。目前外殼與電路板僅有 CAD 與佈線設計，製作及完整組裝尚未完成，因此我們尚未量測平台的耗電量或雜訊表現，也尚不清楚相較於生物層（培養基、耗材、冷鏈）的淨環境足跡。驗證規劃分為五個階段——元件台架測試、純電子鎖相、螢光染劑校正、環境雜訊穩健性、活細胞端到端驗證——目前尚未完成。 下一步：製作並組裝電路板，接著在每個階段完成時，報告實測的雜訊抑制、串擾與功耗。","SDG 12 — Responsible Consumption and Production":"SDG 12——負責任的消費與生產","Non-destructive, reusable-cartridge screening reduces the produce, reagents, and consumables wasted by destructive testing, and prevents good produce from being discarded on suspicion alone.":"非破壞性、使用可重複使用感測匣的篩檢，能減少破壞性檢測所浪費的農產品、試劑與耗材，並避免良好農產品僅因懷疑就遭到丟棄。","Target 12.3 — Food loss. Spoilage often means discarding a whole batch once contamination is visible, days after the VOC signal first appeared. At the household end of the stored-food theme, our public survey [5] points to a related problem. Most respondents (78%) understood that removing visible mold does not always make food safe, but only 58% understood that a normal look and smell does not mean no risk, with 27% unsure and 15% holding the misconception. People who judge by sight and smell will either throw away food that may be fine or keep food that is not. A tool that can say \"this portion is still fine\" cuts needless waste just as flagging real risk cuts unsafe consumption; we treat both as one design problem, hence risk tiers. We have not measured how much food households or businesses actually discard, and the survey is self-reported by people who chose to respond, so it shows where to look rather than how common each belief is. Next step: add the perspective of shops and warehouses, and test the tier output with real users.":"目標 12.3——食物損失。腐敗往往意味著在污染變得可見時丟棄整個批次，而此時距離 VOC 訊號首次出現已過了數天。在儲存食品主題的家庭端，我們的公眾問卷 [5] 指向一個相關問題。多數受訪者（78%）理解移除可見黴菌並不一定能讓食物變得安全，但只有 58% 理解外觀與氣味正常並不代表沒有風險，另有 27% 不確定、15% 抱持錯誤觀念。憑視覺與嗅覺判斷的人，可能會丟掉原本沒有問題的食物，或留下其實有問題的食物。一項能說出「這部分仍然沒有問題」的工具能減少不必要的浪費，正如標示真正風險能減少不安全的食用；我們將兩者視為同一個設計問題，因此採用風險分級。我們尚未量測家庭或企業實際丟棄多少食物，而問卷是由自行選擇參與的人自我回報，因此它指出值得關注的方向，而非每種看法的普遍程度。 下一步：加入商店與倉庫的觀點，並與實際使用者測試分級輸出。","Target 12.5 — Waste prevention and reuse. Destructive assays (PCR, ELISA, GC-MS sample prep) consume the sample and generate single-use chemical waste per test. Our cartridge is designed to be non-destructive and reusable across multiple readings. A self-renewing cell population should need replacing less often than conventional e-nose sensors, some of which the industry says need near-daily replacement — but we have not validated this, and we claim no net environmental benefit until we have. Next step: a cartridge lifetime test, then a simple screening LCA against a destructive-assay baseline; recyclable or biodegradable housing to be evaluated.":"目標 12.5——廢棄物預防與再利用。破壞性檢測（PCR、ELISA、GC-MS 樣品前處理）會消耗樣品，且每次檢測都會產生一次性化學廢棄物。我們的感測匣設計為非破壞性，並可重複進行多次讀取。能夠自我更新的細胞群，其更換頻率應低於傳統電子鼻感測器；據業界所述，某些傳統感測器幾乎每天都需要更換——但我們尚未驗證這一點，在完成驗證之前，也不宣稱具有淨環境效益。 下一步：進行感測匣壽命測試，接著以破壞性檢測為基準，完成簡單的初步生命週期評估；並評估可回收或可生物分解的外殼。","Target 12.4 — Chemicals and waste over the life cycle. We have not yet quantified our own wet-lab footprint (reagents, culture consumables, single-use plastics). Previous iGEM teams have published such self-audits, and we will follow them: classify reagents by hazard, quantify plastic and consumable waste, and identify where segregation or reuse is possible. [Insert audit figures once collected — e.g. approximate plastic waste in kg, reagents by hazard class, existing reuse practices.]Next step: complete the audit before the wiki freeze.":"目標 12.4——生命週期中的化學品與廢棄物。我們尚未量化自身濕實驗室的環境足跡（試劑、培養耗材、一次性塑膠）。過去的 iGEM 團隊曾發表這類自我稽核，我們將循其做法：依危害分類試劑、量化塑膠與耗材廢棄物，並找出可分類處理或再利用之處。 [待蒐集完成後插入稽核數字——例如塑膠廢棄物的約略公斤數、依危害類別分類的試劑、現有再利用做法。]下一步：在 wiki 凍結前完成稽核。","Target 17.16 / 17.17 — Multi-stakeholder partnerships that share knowledge, expertise, and resources.":"目標 17.16／17.17——分享知識、專業能力與資源的多方利害關係人夥伴關係。","Details of each conversation are on our Human Practices page; here we only separate partnerships by maturity, so that exchanges are not presented as partnerships:":"每次對話的詳細內容均列於 Human Practices 頁面；此處僅依成熟度區分夥伴關係，以避免將交流呈現為合作夥伴關係：","Maturity":"成熟度","Who":"對象","Field":"田野","Taoyuan District Agricultural Improvement Station; Taiwan Banana Research Institute; farmers' associations; facility farms":"桃園區農業改良場；財團法人台灣香蕉研究所；農會；設施農場","Shaped the beachhead and our Target 2.3/2.4 reasoning":"形塑切入市場，以及我們對目標 2.3／2.4 的推理","Academic":"學術","Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo (NTHU) and Prof. Ching-Che Charng (China Medical University), co-authors of the paper behind our classifier [10]":"羅中泉教授（清華大學）與張景哲教授（中國醫藥大學），兩位皆為我們分類器基礎論文 [10] 的共同作者","A research partnership in the published sense; Prof. Charng also hosted our September 23 lecture":"已共同發表研究的學術合作關係；張教授也主持了我們 9 月 23 日的演講","Industry":"產業","E-nose company CSO; Chia-Nien Biotechnology; analytical-instrumentation professional; a patent attorney":"電子鼻公司首席科學官；Chia-Nien Biotechnology；分析儀器專業人士；專利律師","Knowledge-sharing only; none is a commercial partnership":"僅為知識分享；沒有任何一項屬於商業合作夥伴關係","iGEM TAU-Israel mini jamboree (October 8); rural elementary-school science camp (October 12); NTHU student workshop (October 14)":"iGEM TAU-Israel mini jamboree（10 月 8 日）；偏鄉國小科學營（10 月 12 日）；清華大學學生工作坊（10 月 14 日）","Exchanges, not yet joint projects":"交流，尚未成為聯合專案","FITI, NTHU Garage+, Hsinchu and Taichung Science Park mentors":"FITI、NTHU Garage+、新竹與臺中科學園區導師","Structured review of our business plan":"有系統地審視我們的商業計畫","Prospective":"潛在合作","Formal discussion with the e-nose company; early talks with the S.Y.Dao Cancer Prevention Foundation":"與電子鼻公司的正式討論；與 S.Y.Dao Cancer Prevention Foundation 的初步對話","No commitment from either side":"雙方均未作出承諾","[Reserved: what the Taiwan Banana Research Institute interview changed or confirmed.]":"[保留待補：財團法人台灣香蕉研究所訪談改變或確認了哪些內容。]","[Reserved: what the other teams' feedback at the mini jamboree changed in our model or education work.]":"[保留待補：mini jamboree 中其他團隊的回饋，改變了我們模型或教育工作的哪些內容。]","Next step: explore whether the CSO conversation can become a formal integration or partnership discussion, and turn one peer-team exchange into a joint activity on food or agriculture.":"下一步：探索與首席科學官的對話是否能發展為正式的整合或合作討論，並將一次與其他團隊的交流轉化為食品或農業主題的聯合活動。","Also connects to":"其他相關連結","SDG 3 — Good Health and Well-being. A detected VOC signal is not a food-safety verdict [8], so AeroSense is a screening tool that recommends confirmatory testing, never a diagnostic replacement. The risk-tier output is the design response. A possible medical direction, raised in early discussions with the S.Y.Dao Cancer Prevention Foundation, is only exploratory: it would bring regulatory demands that our current agricultural and food screening does not face.":"SDG 3——良好健康與福祉。偵測到的 VOC 訊號並不等於食品安全判決 [8]，因此 AeroSense 是建議進行確認性檢測的篩檢工具，絕不取代診斷。風險分級輸出是我們在設計上的回應。在與 S.Y.Dao Cancer Prevention Foundation 的初步討論中提出的潛在醫療方向，目前僅屬探索性質：它將帶來現階段農業與食品篩檢尚未面對的法規要求。","SDG 4 — Quality Education. Our education work targets the specific misunderstanding the survey found, not a general warning that mold is dangerous. It includes a free online learning platform of five short modules, a science camp for upper-grade pupils at a rural elementary school, a university workshop, and a reusable teacher toolkit so that others can run the same sessions without us. We do not yet have completed learning-outcome data, and we will report results as measured.":"SDG 4——優質教育。我們的教育工作針對問卷發現的特定誤解，而非泛泛地警告黴菌具有危險性。內容包括由五個短模組構成的免費線上學習平台、供偏鄉國小高年級學生參與的科學營、大學工作坊，以及可重複使用的教師工具包，讓其他人無須我們到場也能進行相同課程。我們尚未取得完整的學習成果數據，並將依實際量測結果進行報告。","SDG 10 — Reduced Inequalities. The farmer-adoption-resistance finding is also an inequality risk: an individual-farmer product would likely reach only well-resourced buyers. Targeting associations and cooperatives is our current response — not yet a validated equitable outcome.":"SDG 10——減少不平等。農民對採用工具的抗拒，也是一種不平等風險：針對個別農民的產品，很可能只觸及資源充裕的買方。以協會與合作社為對象，是我們目前的回應——尚非經驗證的公平成果。","Limitations and tensions":"限制與矛盾","Our own waste (SDG 12). Living-cell cartridges are themselves a consumable. Lower replacement frequency is our hypothesis; only the LCA can confirm a net benefit.":"我們自身的廢棄物（SDG 12）。活細胞感測匣本身就是耗材。更低的更換頻率是我們的假設；只有生命週期評估能確認淨效益。","Who benefits from innovation (SDG 9 vs. SDG 2/10). Patents are necessary for commercial defensibility, and we are preparing a filing through our university. But restrictive licensing could limit affordability and decide whether exporters or smallholder-serving associations get access.":"誰從創新中受益（SDG 9 與 SDG 2／10）。專利對維持商業競爭防禦能力是必要的，我們正在透過大學準備申請。但限制性的授權可能降低可負擔性，並決定究竟是出口商，還是服務小農的協會能夠取得技術。","Open science vs. patent timing. Our patent attorney advised that our own early disclosure can later count against novelty, so we are holding back some technical detail until a filing is made. This sits uneasily with iGEM's open-science norms and with our wish to leave reusable work for future teams. We resolve it by sequencing — file first, then publish — and by keeping our education materials fully open, because they do not depend on that detail.":"開放科學與專利時程。我們的專利律師提醒，自身過早揭露的內容，日後可能對新穎性不利，因此我們暫緩公開部分技術細節，直到完成申請。這與 iGEM 的開放科學規範，以及我們希望為未來團隊留下可再利用成果的心願之間，存在矛盾。我們透過安排先後次序——先申請，再公開——來處理，並將教育材料維持完全開放，因為它們不依賴那些技術細節。","Partnership maturity (SDG 17). Presenting every interview as a partnership would overstate how far our validation has gone; hence the maturity table above.":"夥伴關係成熟度（SDG 17）。將每次訪談都呈現為夥伴關係，會誇大我們的驗證進展，因此才有上述成熟度表格。","Resilience vs. equity (SDG 2). A tool that makes exporters more resilient can still fail smallholders if the economics do not flow downstream. We do not assume the two move together.":"韌性與公平（SDG 2）。若經濟效益沒有往下游流動，一項能提高出口商韌性的工具，仍可能無法幫助小農。我們不假定兩者會同步提升。","Measuring our contribution":"衡量我們的貢獻","Only the measurements that decide whether the sustainability claims above hold. Everything else is in the Engineering and Human Practices pages.":"此處只列出用來判斷上述永續性主張是否成立的量測。其他內容均列於 Engineering 與 Human Practices 頁面。","Metric":"指標","Baseline":"基準","Detection lead time vs. visual symptom onset":"相對於可見症狀出現的偵測提前時間","0 days (visual sampling)":"0 天（目視抽樣）","[X] days, set after live-cell validation":"[X] 天，於活細胞驗證後設定","Near-daily (conventional e-nose, per industry)":"幾乎每天（傳統電子鼻，據業界所述）","[X] days, from a lifetime test":"[X] 天，由壽命測試得出","Power of the full reader":"完整讀取器的功耗","Measured value, once the board is built":"電路板完成後取得實測值","Wet-lab footprint (reagent hazard classes, plastic kg)":"濕實驗室環境足跡（試劑危害類別、塑膠公斤數）","None":"無","Audit complete before wiki freeze":"在 wiki 凍結前完成稽核","Screening LCA vs. destructive-assay baseline":"相對於破壞性檢測基準的初步生命週期評估","One completed comparison":"完成一次比較","Social. Priority beneficiaries are smallholder farmers and the cooperatives that serve them. The plan is to keep the institution-level buyer model, keep the tool a screening aid rather than a verdict, and use plain-language risk tiers so that farmers and households can act on the result. On the education side, we leave free, reusable materials so that teachers and other teams can run the same sessions without us.":"社會面。優先受益者是小農及服務他們的合作社。計畫是維持機構層級的買方模式，將工具維持為篩檢輔助而非判決，並採用淺白易懂的風險分級，讓農民與家庭能根據結果採取行動。在教育方面，我們留下免費且可重複使用的材料，讓教師與其他團隊無須我們到場，也能進行相同課程。","Economic. Earlier detection targets a sector-level risk of about NT$3.51 billion/year. Before claiming savings, we need the exporter/packing-house interview and a cost model. Commercial staging follows our Entrepreneurship page: banana and mango first, tea second.":"經濟面。提早偵測針對的是每年約新臺幣 35.1 億元的產業層級風險。在宣稱節省成本之前，我們需要完成出口商／包裝場訪談與成本模型。商業階段安排依循 Entrepreneurship 頁面：先香蕉與芒果，再茶葉。","Environmental. The aim is less food discarded and less single-use assay waste. The claim is conditional on the LCA and lifetime test, which will show whether a living-cell cartridge is a net gain.":"環境面。目標是減少遭丟棄的食物與一次性檢測廢棄物。這項主張以生命週期評估及壽命測試為條件，兩者將顯示活細胞感測匣是否帶來淨效益。","For future teams. We document the open items above so that next season's team, or another team, can pick them up directly.":"給未來的團隊。我們記錄上述尚待處理的項目，讓下一季團隊或其他團隊能夠直接接續。","Conclusion":"結論","AeroSense advances agricultural resilience, technological capability, and cross-sector partnership in some respects, and leaves open questions for others: its own cartridge waste, who benefits from patented innovation, how open science and patent timing fit together, and whether resilience reaches smallholders. We have named these trade-offs, tied each to a metric and a next step, and kept a clear line between what is validated and what is intended.":"AeroSense 在某些方面推進農業韌性、技術能力與跨領域夥伴關係，同時仍留下其他未解問題：自身的感測匣廢棄物、誰從專利創新中受益、開放科學與專利時程如何相容，以及韌性是否能到達小農。我們已明確指出這些取捨，為每一項連結指標與下一步，並清楚區分已驗證的內容與預期目標。","References":"參考文獻","[1] World Commission on Environment and Development (1987). Our Common Future. Oxford University Press.":"[1] World Commission on Environment and Development (1987). Our Common Future. Oxford University Press.","[2] United Nations (2015). Transforming Our World: The 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development.":"[2] United Nations (2015). Transforming Our World: The 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development.","[3] Meadows, D. H. (2008). Thinking in Systems: A Primer. Chelsea Green.":"[3] Meadows, D. H. (2008). Thinking in Systems: A Primer. Chelsea Green.","[4] FAO (2019). The State of Food and Agriculture 2019: Moving forward on food loss and waste reduction. Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations.":"[4] FAO (2019). The State of Food and Agriculture 2019: Moving forward on food loss and waste reduction. Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations.","[5] NTHU iGEM 2026 AeroSense Bio. Public Survey — Food Storage Habits and Mold Risk Perception. Team documentation.":"[5] NTHU iGEM 2026 AeroSense Bio. Public Survey — Food Storage Habits and Mold Risk Perception. Team documentation.","[6] NTHU iGEM 2026 AeroSense Bio. Mentor review and field interviews with the Taoyuan District Agricultural Improvement Station and farmers' associations, 2026. Team documentation.":"[6] NTHU iGEM 2026 AeroSense Bio. Mentor review and field interviews with the Taoyuan District Agricultural Improvement Station and farmers' associations, 2026. Team documentation.","[7] NTHU iGEM 2026 AeroSense Bio. Electronic-Nose Industry Interview (Chief Science Officer), 2026. Team documentation.":"[7] NTHU iGEM 2026 AeroSense Bio. Electronic-Nose Industry Interview (Chief Science Officer), 2026. Team documentation.","[8] NTHU iGEM 2026 AeroSense Bio. Chia-Nien Biotechnology Industry Interview — Pathogen-VOC Target Assessment, September 2026. Team documentation.":"[8] NTHU iGEM 2026 AeroSense Bio. Chia-Nien Biotechnology Industry Interview — Pathogen-VOC Target Assessment, September 2026. Team documentation.","[9] NTHU iGEM 2026 AeroSense Bio. Analytical-Instrumentation Industry Interview — Positioning and Competitive Analysis, September 2026. Team documentation.":"[9] NTHU iGEM 2026 AeroSense Bio. Analytical-Instrumentation Industry Interview — Positioning and Competitive Analysis, September 2026. Team documentation.","[10] Cheng, L.-S., Charng, C.-C., Chen, R.-H., Feng, K.-L., Chiang, A.-S., Lo, C.-C., & Lee, T.-K. (2025). Hybrid neural networks in the mushroom body drive olfactory preference in Drosophila. Science Advances, 11(22), eadq9893.":"[10] Cheng, L.-S., Charng, C.-C., Chen, R.-H., Feng, K.-L., Chiang, A.-S., Lo, C.-C., & Lee, T.-K. (2025). Hybrid neural networks in the mushroom body drive olfactory preference in Drosophila. Science Advances, 11(22), eadq9893.","Source:":"來源：","Supporting interactive tools and evidence records":"補充互動工具與證據紀錄","The full source text is above. These supplementary tools retain the wiki’s evidence links, current build notes, and reusable templates.":"上方為完整來源正文。這些補充工具保留 wiki 的證據連結、目前製作紀錄與可重複使用的範本。","Supporting tools and records":"補充工具與紀錄","Read the full pathway ↗":"閱讀完整路徑 ↗","Select the full pathway for targets, evidence and limits.":"選擇完整路徑，查看目標、證據與限制。","Showing detail:":"目前顯示：","Copied":"已複製","Template copied to clipboard.":"範本已複製到剪貼簿。","Copy failed — select the blank canvas text and copy manually.":"複製失敗；請選取空白畫布文字並手動複製。","all":"全部","evidence":"證據","plan":"規劃","gap":"缺口","measured":"實測","stakeholder":"利害關係人支持","estimated":"估算","designed":"設計","hypothesis":"假說","SDG 2 and SDG 12":"SDG 2 與 SDG 12","SDG 3 and SDG 12":"SDG 3 與 SDG 12","SDG 2 and SDG 10":"SDG 2 與 SDG 10","SDG 9 and SDG 10":"SDG 9 與 SDG 10","SDG 9 and SDG 12":"SDG 9 與 SDG 12","SDG 2 and SDG 3":"SDG 2 與 SDG 3","SDG 2 and SDG 9":"SDG 2 與 SDG 9","SDG 3 and SDG 17":"SDG 3 與 SDG 17","SDG 9 and SDG 17":"SDG 9 與 SDG 17","SDG 10 and SDG 17":"SDG 10 與 SDG 17","SDG 2 and SDG 17":"SDG 2 與 SDG 17","SDG 12 and SDG 17":"SDG 12 與 SDG 17","Benefits, burdens and evidence":"效益、負擔與證據","One connected system":"彼此相連的系統","Four goals, four tests":"四項目標，四項驗證","Each goal links a design choice to a benefit hypothesis and the test needed to evaluate it.":"每項目標都連結設計選擇、效益假設與驗證方法。","Sharing knowledge responsibly":"負責任的知識共享","Select a stage or actor to trace a possible benefit, its cost and the available evidence. Engagement labels distinguish interviews, mentorship and formal partnerships.":"選取階段或角色，追溯可能的效益、代價與現有證據。交流標籤區分訪談、指導及正式合作。","Feedback into design":"將回饋轉為設計","Four impact pathways":"四條影響路徑","Each pathway connects an SDG target, the problem, our proposed mechanism, supporting evidence, risks and the next measurement.":"每條路徑連結 SDG 目標、問題、預期機制、支持證據、風險與下一項量測。","Evidence ledger":"證據清單","Survey analysis: reported n = 107":"問卷分析：回報 n = 107","Unverified discard rate":"待核對的丟棄比例","Taiwan banana disease estimate":"臺灣香蕉病害估算","Stakeholder-driven design changes":"回饋促成的設計改變","Grower adoption concerns":"農民採用顧慮","Standalone ESP32 reader design":"獨立 ESP32 讀取器設計","Risk tiers for screening":"篩檢風險分級","Proposed cartridge reuse":"預期的匣體重複使用","Food-loss reduction hypothesis":"減少食物損失的假設","Cartridge lifetime hypothesis":"匣體壽命假設","Fungal VOC sensing hypothesis":"真菌 VOC 感測假設","Unmeasured operating power":"尚未量測的運作功耗","Field readiness":"現場應用成熟度","Toxin and food-safety claims":"毒素與食品安全主張","Patent and operating freedom":"專利與實施自由","Buyer validation":"買方驗證","Measuring net benefit":"衡量淨效益","Life-cycle inventory":"生命週期盤查","Access and equity":"可及性與公平性","Priority measurements":"優先量測項目","Unchecked items are pending measurements.":"未勾選項目表示量測尚待完成。","Other teams can reuse this framework to connect a proposed benefit to evidence, costs and the next measurement.":"其他隊伍可沿用此框架，將預期效益連結到證據、成本與下一項量測。","Copy the framework to your notebook or wiki.":"將框架複製到筆記本或 wiki。","Select a marked relationship to examine a synergy, trade-off or unresolved question. Blank cells indicate that this project has not established a relationship.":"選取已標記的關係，查看協同效益、取捨或尚未解決的問題。空白格表示本專題尚未建立該項關係。","This inventory defines AeroSense’s resource use and waste streams.":"本盤查界定 AeroSense 的資源使用與廢棄物流。","Unmeasured quantities are marked":"未量測的數值標為","This inventory defines AeroSense’s resource use and waste streams. This is a system-boundary inventory —":"本盤查界定 AeroSense 的資源使用與廢棄物流。這是系統邊界盤查，","a completed life-cycle assessment. Unmeasured quantities are marked":"是已完成的生命週期評估。未量測的數值標為","Evidence, limits and next step":"證據、限制與下一步","Analysis pending":"分析待完成","Source unverified":"來源待核實","Primary source pending":"待補原始來源","Buyer test pending":"買方驗證待完成","Performance pending":"效能待驗證","User test pending":"使用者測試待完成","Reuse validation pending":"重複使用待驗證","Pilot pending":"試點待完成","Lifetime test pending":"壽命測試待完成","Response data pending":"待補反應資料","LCA pending":"生命週期評估待完成","Power test pending":"功耗測試待完成","Validation pending":"待驗證","Outside scope":"不在目前主張範圍","Legal review pending":"法律審查待完成","Buyer validation pending":"買方驗證待完成","Sustainability evidence ledger":"永續證據表","Evidence for each sustainability claim. Expand a claim for its sources, interpretation limits and next measurement.":"各項永續主張的證據。展開主張可查看來源、判讀限制與下一項量測。","Status":"狀態","Measured = observed; stakeholder-backed = reported input; estimated = calculation; designed = specification; hypothesis = proposed effect; future work = open evidence gap.":"已量測＝觀察結果；利害關係人支持＝回報意見；估計＝計算；已設計＝規格；假說＝提出的效果；後續工作＝證據缺口。","HEK293 receptor cultures need media and biosafety handling; culture waste and inactivated material follow institutional procedures.":"HEK293 受體培養需要培養液與生物安全處理；培養廢棄物及去活化材料依機構程序處理。","Tips, tubes and plates used in construct development and testing.":"構築開發與測試使用的吸頭、試管及培養盤。","Modular, repeated-read cartridges are a design intent; material, mass and usable lifetime require measurement.":"模組化、可多次讀取的感測匣是設計目標；材料、質量與可用壽命需量測。","ESP32 reader boards, batteries and failed prototypes require a mass inventory and an end-of-life route.":"ESP32 讀取器電路板、電池及失敗原型需建立質量盤查與報廢流程。","Electricity and computation":"電力與運算","Screening information":"篩檢資訊","Optical readout and edge computation are designed to inform follow-up decisions; reader and laboratory energy belong in the same inventory.":"光學讀取與邊緣運算旨在提供後續決策資訊；讀取器與實驗室能源使用應納入同一盤查。","Storage, transport and cleaning":"儲存、運輸與清潔","Maintenance and replacement":"維護與更換","Culture conditions, cold-chain needs, cleaning and reuse protocols remain part of the validation plan.":"培養條件、冷鏈需求、清潔及重複使用程序仍屬驗證計畫。","AeroSense resource and waste inventory":"AeroSense 資源與廢棄物盤查","Resource inputs, outputs and validation needs":"資源投入、產出與驗證需求","Input":"投入","Output":"產出","Note":"說明","These streams are identified but unquantified; net environmental benefit requires a measured life-cycle comparison.":"這些物質與能源流已辨識，但尚未量化；環境淨效益仍需以實測的生命週期比較判定。","Full inventory and process boundaries":"完整盤查與流程邊界","Footprint measurements still needed":"待補足跡量測","The impact framework compares earlier screening with unnecessary discard and the material burden of living-cell cartridges.":"影響評估架構比較提早篩檢、不必要丟棄及活細胞匣的材料負擔。","Pricing and licensing affect whether smaller producers can access the technology.":"定價及授權方式影響小型生產者能否取得技術。","The screening workflow directs concerning samples to confirmatory testing.":"篩檢流程將需注意的樣本導向確認檢測。","Agricultural and sensor-industry interviews focused the innovation effort on biological recognition.":"農業與感測業界訪談使創新工作聚焦於生物辨識。","Biotechnology-industry feedback shaped how we communicate screening results.":"生物科技業界回饋改變了我們溝通篩檢結果的方式。","Sensor-industry critique prioritized selectivity, reproducibility and sensing-element lifetime.":"感測業界意見使我們優先處理選擇性、再現性與感測元件壽命。","Analytical-instrumentation feedback shifted the buyer model toward associations and certification organizations.":"分析儀器業界回饋使買方定位轉向協會與認證機構。","Agricultural-institution interviews and mentor review shaped the banana-export business case.":"農業機構訪談與導師評議形塑了香蕉出口商業定位。","Laboratory design and the 28-response teaching-design survey.":"實驗室設計與 28 份回覆的教學設計問卷。","The 28-response survey shaped food-decision teaching. Education contains the counts and method.":"28 份回覆的問卷形塑食物判斷教學；計數與方法集中於 Education。","Stakeholder input shaped shared access, biological recognition and the screening workflow.":"利害關係人意見形塑了共享使用、生物辨識與篩檢流程。","Buyer model":"買方模型","Risk-tier communication connects a screening result to a confirmatory action.":"風險分級溝通將篩檢結果連結至確認行動。","Producers, agricultural institutions and the export supply-chain roles mapped in Entrepreneurship.":"生產者、農業機構及 Entrepreneurship 所整理的出口供應鏈角色。","Living OR/Orco reporter cells connect to the ESP32 FDM/DLIA optical reader architecture.":"活 OR／Orco 報導細胞連結至 ESP32 FDM／DLIA 光學讀取架構。","The public survey and Challenge Bioproducts interview informed the communication design.":"公眾問卷與 Challenge Bioproducts 訪談提供溝通設計依據。","Electronic-nose industry interview":"電子鼻業界訪談","Living cells add containment and consumable requirements. Pricing and licensing also affect access.":"活細胞增加圍堵與耗材需求；定價及授權也影響使用機會。","The architecture combines headspace sensing, modular cartridges and risk-tier communication. The footprint inventory includes cartridge replacement.":"架構結合頂空感測、模組化細胞匣與風險分級溝通；足跡清單納入細胞匣更換。","Human Practices records how external feedback changed the project.":"Human Practices 記錄外部回饋如何改變專案。","Risk-tier communication connects screening to confirmatory testing.":"風險分級溝通將篩檢連結至確認檢測。","Benefits may remain concentrated at the buyer.":"利益可能集中於買方。","Cartridge and culture waste, containment, energy use and electronics form the resource inventory.":"耗材與培養廢棄物、圍堵、能源及電子設備構成資源盤查範圍。","Design basis: survey findings and stakeholder interviews.":"設計依據：問卷結果與利害關係人訪談。","Interviews shifted the buyer hypothesis toward associations, stations, cooperatives and certifiers.":"訪談使買方假設轉向協會、工作站、合作社及驗證單位。","Potential benefit: earlier isolation and more informed discard decisions.":"潛在效益：提早隔離，並讓丟棄決策更有依據。","Potential benefits, access barriers and supporting inputs by stakeholder group.":"各利害關係群體的潛在效益、使用障礙及支持依據。","28-response teaching-design survey":"28 份回覆的教學設計問卷","The 28-response survey informed teaching decisions; quantified impact uses the model below.":"28 份問卷回覆形成教學決策；量化影響採用下列模型。","Application hypothesis":"應用假設","pain framing · exporter workflow":"痛點界定 · 出口商流程","for buyer shift · for field performance & LCA":"用於買方定位調整 · 用於田間表現與生命週期評估","28 responses shaped the teaching design":"28 份回覆形成教學設計","Public users need clear food-risk information. The 28-response survey informed teaching design.":"一般民眾需要清楚的食物風險資訊；28 份問卷回覆形成教學設計。","Food storage habits and mold-risk perception · 28 responses · 23 August 2026":"食物儲存習慣與黴菌風險認知 · 28 份回覆 · 2026 年 8 月 23 日","Our approach":"我們的方法","Four SDGs at a glance":"四項永續發展目標總覽","Food decision pathway":"食品決策路徑","What we heard":"我們聽到的意見","Supporting goals":"支援目標","Interactions and tensions":"互動與取捨","Our own footprint":"我們自身的環境足跡","Future team toolkit":"未來團隊工具包","Sustainability content":"永續發展內容","Partnerships by maturity":"依成熟度分類的夥伴關係"});
